IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively): section 2026 of the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2026), "Research, demonstration,
-- and evaluations", lines 2392-2654 of usc07-ch51.txt (snap6's first range).
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the OLRC's USLM XML. It is not the official text, and
-- nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- READING A RESULT: a MAYBE BOOLEAN, MAYBE NUMBER or MAYBE DATE answers JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words,
-- JUST TRUE where it says yes, and NOTHING everywhere else ("not covered"). Every branch says which kind it is.
-- MONEY is a NUMBER of dollars. A PERCENTAGE input is a figure in percent: 10 means ten percent. DATES are `Date day month year`.
-- This section is mostly addressed to the Secretary and to State agencies, so most of it is regulative rules and decisions over
-- facts. The household appears in (a)(2), (b)(1)(B)(vi), (b)(1)(C), (d) and (h) to (i).
-- "The State" and "States" are put on `the State agency`, the only State-side party in the core (fork FR-26-1); the Committees,
-- the Secretary of Health and Human Services and the Comptroller General have no party in the core (NEEDS-CORE.md), so duties
-- to report to them are decisions over facts.
-- SEAMS: what other sections answer is taken as an input named for the answering section (SEAMS.md).

-- HELPERS (not a rule of the Act): three-valued AND / OR over MAYBE BOOLEAN, so that a NOTHING input is passed through
-- unless another limb decides the answer without it (PLAN.md section 4).
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026 every one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) xs THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): one limb is the text's no, so the whole is, wherever that no came from
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb says no
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: every limb holds

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026 at least one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) xs THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: one limb holds
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb holds
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): every limb is the text's no

§ `s 2026 -- Research, demonstration, and evaluations`

-- the acts the Secretary, the State agency and the households are told to do or may do, for the regulative rules.
DECLARE `s 2026 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 enter into contracts with or make grants to organizations or agencies to undertake research`
    `s 2026 permit not more than two State agencies to issue aggregate allotments`
    `s 2026 conduct a pilot or experimental project`
    `s 2026 respond to a request for a waiver`
    `s 2026 give the Committees a copy of the denied request and the reasons for the denial`
    `s 2026 conduct a demonstration project to test coordination with the Job Opportunities and Basic Skills program`
    `s 2026 publish the terms and conditions of a demonstration project and notify the Committees`
    `s 2026 develop and implement measures for evaluating the program`
    `s 2026 implement pilot programs to test ways of measuring the nutritional status of low income people`
    `s 2026 report on the pilot programs to the Committees`
    `s 2026 pay the State the value of the allotments`
    `s 2026 pay the cost of the increase in cash benefits`
    `s 2026 provide a written evaluation of the impact of cash assistance`
    `s 2026 conduct a study of the effects of the reductions in benefits`
    `s 2026 conduct a pilot project on intelligent benefit cards`
    `s 2026 carry out studies of the effectiveness of employment and training programs`
    `s 2026 conduct demonstration projects on vehicle exclusion limits`
    `s 2026 conduct projects to test resource accumulation`
    `s 2026 use funds for demonstration projects directed at benefit trafficking`
    `s 2026 carry out pilot projects on health and nutrition promotion`
    `s 2026 enter into contracts or cooperative agreements, or provide grants, for the pilot projects`
    `s 2026 provide for an independent evaluation of the pilot projects`
    `s 2026 pay the costs of monitoring and evaluating a pilot project`
    `s 2026 share the evaluation results broadly`
    `s 2026 make available the mandatory funding for the pilot project`
    `s 2026 cooperate with officials and contractors acting on behalf of the Secretary`
    `s 2026 submit information to the Secretary`
    `s 2026 conduct an independent evaluation of the child support cooperation requirements`
    `s 2026 provide information to the Secretary for the evaluation`
    `s 2026 establish a longitudinal database`
    `s 2026 complete the preparations before approving longitudinal databases`
    `s 2026 protect the privacy of household members in the longitudinal database`
    `s 2026 make the longitudinal database data available to researchers and the Secretary`
    `s 2026 approve the establishment of a longitudinal database`
    `s 2026 provide grants to approved States`
    `s 2026 use funds to carry out the longitudinal database subsection`
    `s 2026 submit the report on the pilot projects to the Committees`
    `s 2026 submit the report on the evaluation of child support cooperation to the Committees`
    `s 2026 submit the report on the feasibility of longitudinal databases to the Committees`

§§ `(a) Contracts or grants; issuance of aggregate allotments`

-- (a)(1) "The Secretary may enter into contracts with or make grants to public or private organizations or agencies under this
-- section to undertake research that will help improve the administration and effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition
-- assistance program in delivering nutrition-related benefits. The waiver authority of the Secretary under subsection (b) shall
-- extend to all contracts and grants under this section."
-- src:2394 | (1) The Secretary may enter into contracts with or make grants to public or private organizations or agencies under this section to undertake research that will help improve the administration and effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in delivering nutrition-related benefits. The waiver authority of the Secretary under subsection (b) shall extend to all contracts and grants under this section.
@ref s 2026(a)(1) contracts and grants (src:2394)
`s 2026(a)(1) the Secretary's permission to enter into contracts or make grants for research` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2026 enter into contracts with or make grants to organizations or agencies to undertake research`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:2394 | (1) The Secretary may enter into contracts with or make grants to public or private organizations or agencies under this section to undertake research that will help improve the administration and effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in delivering nutrition-related benefits. The waiver authority of the Secretary under subsection (b) shall extend to all contracts and grants under this section.
@ref s 2026(a)(1) the waiver authority extends (src:2394)
GIVEN `the instrument is a contract or grant under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(a)(1) the waiver authority of subsection (b) extends to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is a contract or grant under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The waiver authority of the Secretary under subsection (b) shall extend to all contracts and grants under this section"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all contracts and grants under this section"

-- (a)(2) "The Secretary may, on application, permit not more than two State agencies to establish procedures that allow households
-- whose monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits do not exceed $20, at their option, to receive, in lieu of their
-- supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for the initial period under section 2017 of this title and their regular
-- allotment in following months, and at intervals of up to 3 months thereafter, aggregate allotments not to exceed $60 and covering
-- not more than 3 months' benefits."
-- src:2395 | (2) The Secretary may, on application, permit not more than two State agencies to establish procedures that allow households whose monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits do not exceed $20, at their option, to receive, in lieu of their supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for the initial period under section 2017 of this title and their regular allotment in following months, and at intervals of up to 3 months thereafter, aggregate allotments not to exceed $60 and covering not more than 3 months’ benefits. The allotments shall be provided in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title (except that no household shall begin to receive combined allotments under this section until it has complied with all applicable verification requirements of section 2020(e)(3) of this title) and (with respect to the first aggregate allotment so issued) within 40 days of the last benefit issuance.
@ref s 2026(a)(2) the Secretary's permission to permit two State agencies (src:2395)
`s 2026(a)(2) the Secretary's permission to permit two State agencies to issue aggregate allotments` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2026 permit not more than two State agencies to issue aggregate allotments`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:2395 | (2) The Secretary may, on application, permit not more than two State agencies to establish procedures that allow households whose monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits do not exceed $20, at their option, to receive, in lieu of their supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for the initial period under section 2017 of this title and their regular allotment in following months, and at intervals of up to 3 months thereafter, aggregate allotments not to exceed $60 and covering not more than 3 months’ benefits. The allotments shall be provided in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title (except that no household shall begin to receive combined allotments under this section until it has complied with all applicable verification requirements of section 2020(e)(3) of this title) and (with respect to the first aggregate allotment so issued) within 40 days of the last benefit issuance.
@ref s 2026(a)(2) how many State agencies (src:2395)
GIVEN `the number of State agencies the Secretary permits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(a)(2) the number of State agencies permitted is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the number of State agencies the Secretary permits` AT MOST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "permit not more than two State agencies"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not more than two State agencies"

-- src:2395 | (2) The Secretary may, on application, permit not more than two State agencies to establish procedures that allow households whose monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits do not exceed $20, at their option, to receive, in lieu of their supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for the initial period under section 2017 of this title and their regular allotment in following months, and at intervals of up to 3 months thereafter, aggregate allotments not to exceed $60 and covering not more than 3 months’ benefits. The allotments shall be provided in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title (except that no household shall begin to receive combined allotments under this section until it has complied with all applicable verification requirements of section 2020(e)(3) of this title) and (with respect to the first aggregate allotment so issued) within 40 days of the last benefit issuance.
@ref s 2026(a)(2) the household and the aggregate allotment (src:2395)
GIVEN `the household's monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the household chooses to receive the aggregate allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate allotment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months' benefits the aggregate allotment covers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(a)(2) the household may receive the aggregate allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the aggregate allotment, in dollars` GREATER THAN 60 OR `the number of months' benefits the aggregate allotment covers` GREATER THAN 3 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "aggregate allotments not to exceed $60 and covering not more than 3 months' benefits"
        IF `the household's monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits, in dollars` GREATER THAN 20 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the procedures are for "households whose monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits do not exceed $20"
        IF NOT `the household chooses to receive the aggregate allotment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at their option"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: households whose benefits do not exceed $20 may, at their option, receive aggregate allotments of up to $60 covering up to 3 months

-- (a)(2) second sentence "The allotments shall be provided in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this
-- title (except that no household shall begin to receive combined allotments under this section until it has complied with all
-- applicable verification requirements of section 2020(e)(3) of this title) and (with respect to the first aggregate allotment so
-- issued) within 40 days of the last benefit issuance."
-- src:2395 | (2) The Secretary may, on application, permit not more than two State agencies to establish procedures that allow households whose monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits do not exceed $20, at their option, to receive, in lieu of their supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for the initial period under section 2017 of this title and their regular allotment in following months, and at intervals of up to 3 months thereafter, aggregate allotments not to exceed $60 and covering not more than 3 months’ benefits. The allotments shall be provided in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title (except that no household shall begin to receive combined allotments under this section until it has complied with all applicable verification requirements of section 2020(e)(3) of this title) and (with respect to the first aggregate allotment so issued) within 40 days of the last benefit issuance.
@ref s 2026(a)(2) verification before combined allotments (src:2395)
GIVEN `s 2020(e)(3) the household has complied with all applicable verification requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(a)(2) the household may begin to receive combined allotments` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2020(e)(3) the household has complied with all applicable verification requirements`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no household shall begin to receive combined allotments under this section until it has complied with all applicable verification requirements"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no household shall ... until" bars and grants nothing; the permission is earlier in the paragraph
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): compliance with section 2020(e)(3) is that section's answer

-- src:2395 | (2) The Secretary may, on application, permit not more than two State agencies to establish procedures that allow households whose monthly supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits do not exceed $20, at their option, to receive, in lieu of their supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for the initial period under section 2017 of this title and their regular allotment in following months, and at intervals of up to 3 months thereafter, aggregate allotments not to exceed $60 and covering not more than 3 months’ benefits. The allotments shall be provided in accordance with paragraphs (3) and (9) of section 2020(e) of this title (except that no household shall begin to receive combined allotments under this section until it has complied with all applicable verification requirements of section 2020(e)(3) of this title) and (with respect to the first aggregate allotment so issued) within 40 days of the last benefit issuance.
@ref s 2026(a)(2) the first aggregate allotment within 40 days (src:2395)
GIVEN `the aggregate allotment is the first so issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the last benefit issuance to the aggregate allotment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(a)(2) the first aggregate allotment was provided in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the aggregate allotment is the first so issued` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(with respect to the first aggregate allotment so issued)"
        IF `days from the last benefit issuance to the aggregate allotment` AT MOST 40 THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "within 40 days of the last benefit issuance"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 40 days of the last benefit issuance"

§§ `(b) Pilot projects`

-- (b)(1)(A) "The Secretary may conduct on a trial basis, in one or more areas of the United States, pilot or experimental projects
-- designed to test program changes that might increase the efficiency of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and
-- improve the delivery of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits to eligible households, and may waive any
-- requirement of this chapter to the extent necessary for the project to be conducted."
-- src:2398 | (A) The Secretary may conduct on a trial basis, in one or more areas of the United States, pilot or experimental projects designed to test program changes that might increase the efficiency of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and improve the delivery of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits to eligible households, and may waive any requirement of this chapter to the extent necessary for the project to be conducted.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(A) pilot or experimental projects (src:2398)
`s 2026(b)(1)(A) the Secretary's permission to conduct a pilot or experimental project` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2026 conduct a pilot or experimental project`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:2398 | (A) The Secretary may conduct on a trial basis, in one or more areas of the United States, pilot or experimental projects designed to test program changes that might increase the efficiency of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and improve the delivery of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits to eligible households, and may waive any requirement of this chapter to the extent necessary for the project to be conducted.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(A) the waiver (src:2398)
GIVEN `the waiver is to the extent necessary for the project to be conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(A) the Secretary may waive the requirement of this chapter` MEANS
    IF `the waiver is to the extent necessary for the project to be conducted`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may waive any requirement of this chapter to the extent necessary for the project to be conducted"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent necessary for the project to be conducted"

-- (b)(1)(B)(i) "The Secretary may not conduct a project under subparagraph (A) unless— (I) the project is consistent with the goal
-- of the supplemental nutrition assistance program of providing food assistance to raise levels of nutrition among low-income
-- individuals; and (II) the project includes an evaluation to determine the effects of the project."
-- src:2400 | (i) Program goal.—
-- src:2401 | The Secretary may not conduct a project under subparagraph (A) unless—
-- src:2402 | (I) the project is consistent with the goal of the supplemental nutrition assistance program of providing food assistance to raise levels of nutrition among low-income individuals; and
-- src:2403 | (II) the project includes an evaluation to determine the effects of the project.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(i) program goal (src:2400-2403)
GIVEN `the project is consistent with the goal of the supplemental nutrition assistance program of providing food assistance to raise levels of nutrition among low-income individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the project includes an evaluation to determine the effects of the project` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(i) the Secretary may conduct the project` MEANS
    IF `the project is consistent with the goal of the supplemental nutrition assistance program of providing food assistance to raise levels of nutrition among low-income individuals` AND `the project includes an evaluation to determine the effects of the project`
    THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may not ... unless" bars and grants nothing; the permission is in subparagraph (A)
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary may not conduct a project under subparagraph (A) unless"

-- (b)(1)(B)(ii) "The Secretary may conduct a project under subparagraph (A) to— (I) improve program administration; (II) increase
-- the self-sufficiency of supplemental nutrition assistance program recipients; (III) test innovative welfare reform strategies; or
-- (IV) allow greater conformity with the rules of other programs than would be allowed but for this paragraph."
DECLARE `s 2026 purpose of a project` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 improve program administration`
    `s 2026 increase the self-sufficiency of supplemental nutrition assistance program recipients`
    `s 2026 test innovative welfare reform strategies`
    `s 2026 allow greater conformity with the rules of other programs`
    `s 2026 some other purpose`

-- src:2404 | (ii) Permissible projects.—
-- src:2405 | The Secretary may conduct a project under subparagraph (A) to—
-- src:2406 | (I) improve program administration;
-- src:2407 | (II) increase the self-sufficiency of supplemental nutrition assistance program recipients;
-- src:2408 | (III) test innovative welfare reform strategies; or
-- src:2409 | (IV) allow greater conformity with the rules of other programs than would be allowed but for this paragraph.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(ii) permissible projects (src:2404-2409)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 2026 purpose of a project`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(ii) the Secretary may conduct the project for the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 2026 some other purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text does not say "only" or "nothing but"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(I) improve program administration; (II) increase the self-sufficiency ...; (III) test innovative welfare reform strategies; or (IV) allow greater conformity with the rules of other programs"

-- (b)(1)(B)(iii) "If the Secretary finds that a project under subparagraph (A) would reduce benefits by more than 20 percent for more
-- than 5 percent of households in the area subject to the project (not including any household whose benefits are reduced due to a
-- failure to comply with work or other conduct requirements), the project— (I) may not include more than 15 percent of the number of
-- households in the State receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits; and (II) shall continue for not more than 5
-- years after the date of implementation, unless the Secretary approves an extension requested by the State agency at any time."
-- src:2411 | If the Secretary finds that a project under subparagraph (A) would reduce benefits by more than 20 percent for more than 5 percent of households in the area subject to the project (not including any household whose benefits are reduced due to a failure to comply with work or other conduct requirements), the project—
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii) when the restrictions apply (src:2411)
GIVEN `the percentage of households in the area whose benefits the project would reduce by more than 20 percent, not counting households reduced for failure to comply with work or other conduct requirements` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii) the restrictions apply to the project` MEANS
    IF `the percentage of households in the area whose benefits the project would reduce by more than 20 percent, not counting households reduced for failure to comply with work or other conduct requirements` GREATER THAN 5
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "If the Secretary finds that a project ... would reduce benefits by more than 20 percent for more than 5 percent of households in the area"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a failed "If" (marginal reading (a))

-- src:2412 | (I) may not include more than 15 percent of the number of households in the State receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits; and
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(I) the share of the State's households (src:2412)
GIVEN `the restrictions apply to the project` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the percentage of the number of households in the State receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits the project includes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(I) the project may include that share of the State's households` MEANS
    IF `the restrictions apply to the project` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the percentage of the number of households in the State receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits the project includes` GREATER THAN 15
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not include more than 15 percent of the number of households in the State" (the input is a number of percent as printed: 15 means 15 percent, and 0.15 would mean 0.15 percent)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for a project the restrictions apply to, and grants nothing; at exactly 15 percent the bar is not triggered

-- src:2413 | (II) shall continue for not more than 5 years after the date of implementation, unless the Secretary approves an extension requested by the State agency at any time.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(II) the length of the project (src:2413)
GIVEN `the restrictions apply to the project` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the years after the date of implementation the project continues` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary approves an extension requested by the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iii)(II) the project may continue` MEANS
    IF `the restrictions apply to the project` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the years after the date of implementation the project continues` GREATER THAN 5 AND NOT `the Secretary approves an extension requested by the State agency`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall continue for not more than 5 years after the date of implementation, unless the Secretary approves an extension"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for a project the restrictions apply to, and grants nothing

-- (b)(1)(B)(iv) "The Secretary may not conduct a project under subparagraph (A) that— (I) involves the payment of the value of an
-- allotment in the form of cash or otherwise providing benefits in a form not restricted to the purchase of food, unless the
-- project was approved prior to August 22, 1996; (II) has the effect of substantially transferring funds ... or using the funds
-- for any purpose other than the purchase of food, program administration, or an employment or training program; (III) is
-- inconsistent with— (aa) to (jj); (IV) modifies the operation of section 2014 ... so as to have the effect of— (aa) increasing
-- the shelter deduction ... or (bb) absolving a State from acting with reasonable promptness ...; (V) is not limited to a specific
-- time period; (VI) waives a provision of section 2035 of this title; or (VII) waives a provision of section 2016(i)."
DECLARE `s 2026 provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 paragraphs (4) and (5) of section 2012(m)`
    `s 2026 the last sentence of section 2014(a), insofar as a waiver denies assistance to an otherwise eligible household or individual who has not failed to comply with any work, behavioral, or other conduct requirement`
    `s 2026 section 2014(c)(2)`
    `s 2026 paragraph (2)(B), (4)(F)(i), or (4)(K) of section 2015(d)`
    `s 2026 section 2017(b)`
    `s 2026 section 2020(e)(2)(B)`
    `s 2026 the time standard under section 2020(e)(3)`
    `s 2026 subsection (a), (c), (g), (h)(1)(F), (h)(2), or (h)(3) of section 2025`
    `s 2026 this paragraph`
    `s 2026 subsection (a)(1) or (g)(1) of section 2029`
    `s 2026 some other provision`

DECLARE `s 2026 project` HAS
    `it involves the payment of the value of an allotment in the form of cash or otherwise provides benefits in a form not restricted to the purchase of food` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the Secretary approved it, if it was approved`                         IS A MAYBE DATE
    `it has the effect of substantially transferring funds made available under this chapter to services or benefits provided primarily through another public assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it uses the funds for a purpose other than the purchase of food, program administration, or an employment or training program` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provisions it is inconsistent with`                                         IS A LIST OF `s 2026 provision`
    `it modifies the operation of section 2014 so as to increase the shelter deduction to households with no out-of-pocket housing costs or housing costs that consume a low percentage of income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it modifies the operation of section 2014 so as to absolve a State from acting with reasonable promptness on substantial reported changes in income or household size, other than changes related to deductions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is not limited to a specific time period`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it waives a provision of section 2035`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it waives a provision of section 2016(i)`                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2415 | The Secretary may not conduct a project under subparagraph (A) that—
-- src:2416 | (I) involves the payment of the value of an allotment in the form of cash or otherwise providing benefits in a form not restricted to the purchase of food, unless the project was approved prior to August 22, 1996;
-- src:2417 | (II) has the effect of substantially transferring funds made available under this chapter to services or benefits provided primarily through another public assistance program, or using the funds for any purpose other than the purchase of food, program administration, or an employment or training program;
-- src:2418 | (III) is inconsistent with—
-- src:2419 | (aa) paragraphs (4) and (5) of section 2012(m) of this title;
-- src:2420 | (bb) the last sentence of section 2014(a) of this title, insofar as a waiver denies assistance to an otherwise eligible household or individual if the household or individual has not failed to comply with any work, behavioral, or other conduct requirement under this or another program;
-- src:2421 | (cc) section 2014(c)(2) of this title;
-- src:2422 | (dd) paragraph (2)(B), (4)(F)(i), or (4)(K) of section 2015(d) of this title;
-- src:2423 | (ee) section 2017(b) of this title;
-- src:2424 | (ff) section 2020(e)(2)(B) of this title;
-- src:2425 | (gg) the time standard under section 2020(e)(3) of this title;
-- src:2426 | (hh) subsection (a), (c), (g), (h)(1)(F), (h)(2), or (h)(3) of section 2025 of this title;
-- src:2427 | (ii) this paragraph; or
-- src:2428 | (jj) subsection (a)(1) or (g)(1) of section 2029 of this title;
-- src:2429 | (IV) modifies the operation of section 2014 of this title so as to have the effect of—
-- src:2430 | (aa) increasing the shelter deduction to households with no out-of-pocket housing costs or housing costs that consume a low percentage of the household’s income; or
-- src:2431 | (bb) absolving a State from acting with reasonable promptness on substantial reported changes in income or household size (except that this subclause shall not apply with regard to changes related to supplemental nutrition assistance program deductions);
-- src:2432 | (V) is not limited to a specific time period;
-- src:2433 | (VI) waives a provision of section 2035 of this title; or
-- src:2434 | (VII) waives a provision of section 2016(i) of this title.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) impermissible projects (src:2415-2434)
GIVEN project IS A `s 2026 project`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv) the Secretary may conduct the project` MEANS
    IF cashNotApproved
       OR project's `it has the effect of substantially transferring funds made available under this chapter to services or benefits provided primarily through another public assistance program`
       OR project's `it uses the funds for a purpose other than the purchase of food, program administration, or an employment or training program`
       OR NOT (null (project's `the provisions it is inconsistent with`))
       OR project's `it modifies the operation of section 2014 so as to increase the shelter deduction to households with no out-of-pocket housing costs or housing costs that consume a low percentage of income`
       OR project's `it modifies the operation of section 2014 so as to absolve a State from acting with reasonable promptness on substantial reported changes in income or household size, other than changes related to deductions`
       OR project's `it is not limited to a specific time period`
       OR project's `it waives a provision of section 2035`
       OR project's `it waives a provision of section 2016(i)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary may not conduct a project under subparagraph (A) that" does any of (I) to (VII)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may not conduct a project that" bars and grants nothing; the permission is in subparagraph (A)
    WHERE
        cashNotApproved MEANS project's `it involves the payment of the value of an allotment in the form of cash or otherwise provides benefits in a form not restricted to the purchase of food` AND NOT approvedBefore
        approvedBefore MEANS
            CONSIDER project's `the date the Secretary approved it, if it was approved`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST d THEN d LESS THAN (Date 22 8 1996)   -- "unless the project was approved prior to August 22, 1996"

-- src:2419 | (aa) paragraphs (4) and (5) of section 2012(m) of this title;
-- src:2420 | (bb) the last sentence of section 2014(a) of this title, insofar as a waiver denies assistance to an otherwise eligible household or individual if the household or individual has not failed to comply with any work, behavioral, or other conduct requirement under this or another program;
-- src:2421 | (cc) section 2014(c)(2) of this title;
-- src:2422 | (dd) paragraph (2)(B), (4)(F)(i), or (4)(K) of section 2015(d) of this title;
-- src:2423 | (ee) section 2017(b) of this title;
-- src:2424 | (ff) section 2020(e)(2)(B) of this title;
-- src:2425 | (gg) the time standard under section 2020(e)(3) of this title;
-- src:2426 | (hh) subsection (a), (c), (g), (h)(1)(F), (h)(2), or (h)(3) of section 2025 of this title;
-- src:2427 | (ii) this paragraph; or
-- src:2428 | (jj) subsection (a)(1) or (g)(1) of section 2029 of this title;
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) a provision the project is inconsistent with (src:2419-2428)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 2026 provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(iv)(III) the provision is one a project may not be inconsistent with` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 2026 some other provision` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the ten items (aa) to (jj) are the provisions the text lists
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(III) is inconsistent with— (aa) ... (jj)"

-- (b)(1)(B)(v) "A pilot or experimental project may include projects involving the payment of the value of allotments or the
-- average value of allotments by household size in the form of cash to eligible households all of whose members are age
-- sixty-five or over or any of whose members are entitled to supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social
-- Security Act or are receiving assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act, the
-- use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household's privacy, and the use of food checks or other voucher-type
-- forms in place of EBT cards."
DECLARE `s 2026 additional included project` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households`
    `s 2026 the use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household's privacy`
    `s 2026 the use of food checks or other voucher-type forms in place of EBT cards`
    `s 2026 some other project`

-- src:2436 | A pilot or experimental project may include projects involving the payment of the value of allotments or the average value of allotments by household size in the form of cash to eligible households all of whose members are age sixty-five or over or any of whose members are entitled to supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1381 et seq.] or are receiving assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), the use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household’s privacy, and the use of food checks or other voucher-type forms in place of EBT cards.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) additional included projects (src:2436)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2026 additional included project`
      `all members of the household are age sixty-five or over` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any member of the household is entitled to supplemental security income benefits under title XVI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any member of the household is receiving assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(v) the project may be included in a pilot or experimental project` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 2026 payment of the value of allotments, or the average value by household size, in cash to eligible households` THEN
        IF `all members of the household are age sixty-five or over` OR `any member of the household is entitled to supplemental security income benefits under title XVI` OR `any member of the household is receiving assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV`
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "payment ... in the form of cash to eligible households all of whose members are age sixty-five or over or any of whose members are entitled to supplemental security income benefits ... or are receiving assistance under a State program funded under part A of title IV"
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): cash payments to "eligible households all of whose members are age sixty-five or over or any of whose members" receive SSI or part A assistance
    WHEN `s 2026 the use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household's privacy` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the use of identification mechanisms that do not invade a household's privacy"
    WHEN `s 2026 the use of food checks or other voucher-type forms in place of EBT cards` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the use of food checks or other voucher-type forms in place of EBT cards"
    WHEN `s 2026 some other project` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may include" does not say "only"

-- (b)(1)(B)(vi) "Subject to the availability of appropriations under section 2027(a) of this title, any pilot or experimental
-- project implemented under this paragraph and operating as of October 1, 1981, involving the payment of the value of allotments
-- in the form of cash to eligible households all of whose members are either age sixty-five or over or entitled to supplemental
-- security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act shall be continued if the State so requests."
-- src:2438 | Subject to the availability of appropriations under section 2027(a) of this title, any pilot or experimental project implemented under this paragraph and operating as of October 1, 1981, involving the payment of the value of allotments in the form of cash to eligible households all of whose members are either age sixty-five or over or entitled to supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act shall be continued if the State so requests.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) cash payment pilot projects (src:2438)
GIVEN `the project was implemented under this paragraph and operating as of October 1, 1981, paying allotments in cash to eligible households all of whose members are age sixty-five or over or entitled to supplemental security income benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State requests that it be continued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2027(a) appropriations are available` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(B)(vi) the project shall be continued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the project was implemented under this paragraph and operating as of October 1, 1981, paying allotments in cash to eligible households all of whose members are age sixty-five or over or entitled to supplemental security income benefits` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any pilot or experimental project implemented under this paragraph and operating as of October 1, 1981"
        IF NOT `the State requests that it be continued` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a failed "if the State so requests" (marginal reading (a))
        IF `s 2027(a) appropriations are available` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall be continued if the State so requests"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to the availability of appropriations under section 2027(a)", which is that section's answer

-- (b)(1)(C) "(i) No waiver or demonstration program shall be approved under this chapter after November 28, 1990, unless— (I) any
-- household whose food assistance is issued in a form other than EBT cards has its allotment increased to the extent necessary to
-- compensate for any State or local sales tax ..., the tax on purchases of food by any such household is waived, or the Secretary
-- determines on the basis of information provided by the State agency that the increase is unnecessary on the basis of the limited
-- nature of the items subject to the State or local sales tax; and (II) the State agency conducting the demonstration project pays
-- the cost of any increased allotments. (ii) Clause (i) shall not apply if a waiver or demonstration project already provides a
-- household with assistance that exceeds that which the household would otherwise be eligible to receive by more than the
-- estimated amount of any sales tax on the purchases of food that would be collected from the household in the project area."
-- src:2440 | (i) No waiver or demonstration program shall be approved under this chapter after November 28, 1990, unless—
-- src:2441 | (I) any household whose food assistance is issued in a form other than EBT cards has its allotment increased to the extent necessary to compensate for any State or local sales tax that may be collected in all or part of the area covered by the demonstration project, the tax on purchases of food by any such household is waived, or the Secretary determines on the basis of information provided by the State agency that the increase is unnecessary on the basis of the limited nature of the items subject to the State or local sales tax; and
-- src:2442 | (II) the State agency conducting the demonstration project pays the cost of any increased allotments.
-- src:2443 | (ii) Clause (i) shall not apply if a waiver or demonstration project already provides a household with assistance that exceeds that which the household would otherwise be eligible to receive by more than the estimated amount of any sales tax on the purchases of food that would be collected from the household in the project area in which the household resides.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(C) sales tax compensation (src:2440-2443)
GIVEN `the date the waiver or demonstration program is approved` IS A DATE
      `a household's food assistance is issued in a form other than EBT cards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is increased to compensate for the sales tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tax on purchases of food by the household is waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that the increase is unnecessary on the basis of the limited nature of the items subject to the tax` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency conducting the demonstration project pays the cost of any increased allotments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the waiver or demonstration project already provides assistance exceeding what the household would otherwise be eligible to receive by more than the estimated sales tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(C) the waiver or demonstration program may be approved` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the waiver or demonstration program is approved` AT MOST (Date 28 11 1990) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after November 28, 1990"
        IF `the waiver or demonstration project already provides assistance exceeding what the household would otherwise be eligible to receive by more than the estimated sales tax` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (ii), "Clause (i) shall not apply if"
        IF ((NOT `a household's food assistance is issued in a form other than EBT cards`) OR `the allotment is increased to compensate for the sales tax` OR `the tax on purchases of food by the household is waived` OR `the Secretary determines that the increase is unnecessary on the basis of the limited nature of the items subject to the tax`) AND `the State agency conducting the demonstration project pays the cost of any increased allotments` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be approved ... unless" bars and grants nothing; the permission is elsewhere
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No waiver or demonstration program shall be approved under this chapter after November 28, 1990, unless" (I) and (II)

-- (b)(1)(D)(i) "Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request for a waiver under subparagraph (A), the Secretary
-- shall provide a response that— (I) approves the waiver request; (II) denies the waiver request and describes any modification
-- needed for approval of the waiver request; (III) denies the waiver request and describes the grounds for the denial; or (IV)
-- requests clarification of the waiver request."
DECLARE `s 2026 response to a waiver request` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 approves the waiver request`
    `s 2026 denies the waiver request and describes any modification needed for approval`
    `s 2026 denies the waiver request and describes the grounds for the denial`
    `s 2026 requests clarification of the waiver request`
    `s 2026 some other response`

-- src:2446 | Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request for a waiver under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall provide a response that—
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary's duty to respond to a waiver request (src:2446)
`s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary's duty to respond to a request for a waiver` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 respond to a request for a waiver`
    WITHIN 60   -- days after the date of receiving the request
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not respond to the request for a waiver within 60 days after receiving it"

-- src:2446 | Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request for a waiver under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall provide a response that—
-- src:2447 | (I) approves the waiver request;
-- src:2448 | (II) denies the waiver request and describes any modification needed for approval of the waiver request;
-- src:2449 | (III) denies the waiver request and describes the grounds for the denial; or
-- src:2450 | (IV) requests clarification of the waiver request.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the response (src:2446-2450)
GIVEN response IS A `s 2026 response to a waiver request`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the response is one the Secretary shall provide` MEANS
    CONSIDER response
    WHEN `s 2026 some other response` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall provide a response that" is one of (I) to (IV)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(I) approves ...; (II) denies ... and describes any modification ...; (III) denies ... and describes the grounds ...; or (IV) requests clarification"

-- src:2446 | Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request for a waiver under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall provide a response that—
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the twin over days (src:2446)
GIVEN `the Secretary has provided a response` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from receiving the request to the response, or to today if none yet` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(D)(i) the Secretary responded in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has provided a response` AND `days from receiving the request to the response, or to today if none yet` AT MOST 60 THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request"
        IF `days from receiving the request to the response, or to today if none yet` GREATER THAN 60 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 60 days after the date of receiving a request" (a time bound read as a no, marginal reading)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no response yet and the 60 days have not run

-- (b)(1)(D)(ii) "If the Secretary does not provide a response in accordance with clause (i), the waiver shall be considered
-- approved, unless the approval is specifically prohibited by this chapter."
-- src:2452 | If the Secretary does not provide a response in accordance with clause (i), the waiver shall be considered approved, unless the approval is specifically prohibited by this chapter.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii) failure to respond (src:2452)
GIVEN `the Secretary provided a response in accordance with clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval is specifically prohibited by this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(D)(ii) the waiver is considered approved` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary provided a response in accordance with clause (i)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a failed "If the Secretary does not provide a response in accordance with clause (i)" (marginal reading (a))
        IF `the approval is specifically prohibited by this chapter` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the approval is specifically prohibited by this chapter"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the waiver shall be considered approved"

-- (b)(1)(D)(iii) "On denial of a waiver request under clause (i)(III), the Secretary shall provide a copy of the waiver request and
-- a description of the reasons for the denial to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on
-- Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate."
-- src:2454 | On denial of a waiver request under clause (i)(III), the Secretary shall provide a copy of the waiver request and a description of the reasons for the denial to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the Secretary's duty to give the Committees the copy (src:2454)
`s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the Secretary's duty to give the Committees a copy of the denied request` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 give the Committees a copy of the denied request and the reasons for the denial`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not give the Committees a copy of the denied request and the reasons for the denial"

-- src:2454 | On denial of a waiver request under clause (i)(III), the Secretary shall provide a copy of the waiver request and a description of the reasons for the denial to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate.
@ref s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the decision (src:2454)
GIVEN `the Secretary denied the request under clause (i)(III)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy and a description of the reasons were provided to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy and a description of the reasons were provided to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(1)(D)(iii) the Secretary has given both Committees the copy and the reasons` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Secretary denied the request under clause (i)(III)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On denial of a waiver request under clause (i)(III)"
        IF `a copy and a description of the reasons were provided to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives` AND `a copy and a description of the reasons were provided to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall provide a copy of the waiver request and a description of the reasons for the denial to the Committee on Agriculture ... and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text sets no time for the copy and says nothing of what follows if it is not given

-- (b)(2)(A) "The Secretary may conduct demonstration projects to test improved consistency or coordination between the supplemental
-- nutrition assistance program employment and training program and the Job Opportunities and Basic Skills program under title IV
-- of the Social Security Act."
-- src:2456 | (A) The Secretary may conduct demonstration projects to test improved consistency or coordination between the supplemental nutrition assistance program employment and training program and the Job Opportunities and Basic Skills program under title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.).
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(A) demonstration projects (src:2456)
`s 2026(b)(2)(A) the Secretary's permission to conduct demonstration projects on employment and training` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2026 conduct a demonstration project to test coordination with the Job Opportunities and Basic Skills program`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (b)(2)(B) "Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Secretary may, as part of a project authorized under this paragraph, waive
-- requirements under section 2015(d) of this title to permit a State to operate an employment and training program ... on the
-- same terms and conditions under which the State operates its Job Opportunities and Basic Skills program ... Any work experience
-- program conducted as part of the project shall be conducted in conformity with section 482(f) of such Act."
-- src:2457 | (B) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Secretary may, as part of a project authorized under this paragraph, waive requirements under section 2015(d) of this title to permit a State to operate an employment and training program for supplemental nutrition assistance program recipients on the same terms and conditions under which the State operates its Job Opportunities and Basic Skills program for recipients of aid to families with dependent children under part F [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 681 et seq.). Any work experience program conducted as part of the project shall be conducted in conformity with section 482(f) of such Act (42 U.S.C. 682(f)).
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(B) waiver of section 2015(d) requirements (src:2457)
GIVEN `the waiver is part of a project authorized under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(2)(B) the Secretary may waive requirements under section 2015(d)` MEANS
    IF `the waiver is part of a project authorized under paragraph (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Secretary may, as part of a project authorized under this paragraph, waive requirements under section 2015(d)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as part of a project authorized under this paragraph"

-- src:2457 | (B) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Secretary may, as part of a project authorized under this paragraph, waive requirements under section 2015(d) of this title to permit a State to operate an employment and training program for supplemental nutrition assistance program recipients on the same terms and conditions under which the State operates its Job Opportunities and Basic Skills program for recipients of aid to families with dependent children under part F [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 681 et seq.). Any work experience program conducted as part of the project shall be conducted in conformity with section 482(f) of such Act (42 U.S.C. 682(f)).
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(B) work experience (src:2457)
GIVEN `the work experience program is conducted as part of the project` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conducted in conformity with section 482(f) of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(2)(B) the work experience program is conducted as the text requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the work experience program is conducted as part of the project` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any work experience program conducted as part of the project"
        IF `it is conducted in conformity with section 482(f) of the Social Security Act` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall be conducted in conformity with section 482(f) of such Act"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the program shall be and not what follows if it is not

-- (b)(2)(C) "A State seeking such a waiver shall provide assurances that the resulting employment and training program shall meet
-- the requirements of subsections (a)(19) and (g) of section 402 of such Act (but not including the provision of transitional
-- benefits under clauses (ii) through (vii) of section 402(g)(1)(A)) and sections 481 through 487 of such Act. Each reference to
-- 'aid to families with dependent children' in such sections shall be deemed to be a reference to supplemental nutrition
-- assistance program benefits for purposes of the demonstration project."
-- src:2458 | (C) A State seeking such a waiver shall provide assurances that the resulting employment and training program shall meet the requirements of subsections (a)(19) and (g) of section 402 1 of such Act (42 U.S.C. 602) (but not including the provision of transitional benefits under clauses (ii) through (vii) of section 402(g)(1)(A) 1) and sections 481 through 487 1 of such Act (42 U.S.C. 681 through 687). Each reference to “aid to families with dependent children” in such sections shall be deemed to be a reference to supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for purposes of the demonstration project.
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(C) assurances (src:2458)
GIVEN `the State seeks such a waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State has provided assurances that the resulting employment and training program shall meet the requirements named` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(2)(C) the State has provided the assurances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State seeks such a waiver` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A State seeking such a waiver"
        IF `the State has provided assurances that the resulting employment and training program shall meet the requirements named` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall provide assurances that the resulting employment and training program shall meet the requirements"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the State shall provide and not what follows if it does not

-- src:2458 | (C) A State seeking such a waiver shall provide assurances that the resulting employment and training program shall meet the requirements of subsections (a)(19) and (g) of section 402 1 of such Act (42 U.S.C. 602) (but not including the provision of transitional benefits under clauses (ii) through (vii) of section 402(g)(1)(A) 1) and sections 481 through 487 1 of such Act (42 U.S.C. 681 through 687). Each reference to “aid to families with dependent children” in such sections shall be deemed to be a reference to supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for purposes of the demonstration project.
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(C) the deemed reference (src:2458)
GIVEN phrase IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 2026(b)(2)(C) what the reference in the sections named is deemed to be` MEANS
    IF phrase EQUALS "aid to families with dependent children"
    THEN JUST "supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits"   -- "Each reference to 'aid to families with dependent children' in such sections shall be deemed to be a reference to supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only that phrase is deemed

-- (b)(2)(D) "Notwithstanding the other provisions of this paragraph, participation in an employment and training activity in which
-- supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits are converted to cash shall occur only with the consent of the participant."
-- src:2459 | (D) Notwithstanding the other provisions of this paragraph, participation in an employment and training activity in which supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits are converted to cash shall occur only with the consent of the participant.
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(D) consent to conversion to cash (src:2459)
GIVEN `the activity is one in which supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits are converted to cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the participant consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(2)(D) the participant may take part in the activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the activity is one in which supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits are converted to cash` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an employment and training activity in which supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits are converted to cash"
        IF `the participant consents` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only with the consent" bars and grants nothing
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall occur only with the consent of the participant"

-- (b)(2)(E) "For the purposes of any project conducted under this paragraph, the provisions of this chapter affecting the rights of
-- recipients may be waived to the extent necessary to conform to the provisions of section 402, and sections 481 through 487, of
-- the Social Security Act."
-- src:2460 | (E) For the purposes of any project conducted under this paragraph, the provisions of this chapter affecting the rights of recipients may be waived to the extent necessary to conform to the provisions of section 402, and sections 481 through 487,1 of the Social Security Act.
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(E) waiver of provisions affecting recipients' rights (src:2460)
GIVEN `the project is conducted under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the waiver is to the extent necessary to conform to section 402 and sections 481 through 487 of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(2)(E) the provisions affecting the rights of recipients may be waived` MEANS
    IF `the project is conducted under paragraph (2)` AND `the waiver is to the extent necessary to conform to section 402 and sections 481 through 487 of the Social Security Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "For the purposes of any project conducted under this paragraph, the provisions ... may be waived to the extent necessary to conform"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any project conducted under this paragraph" and "to the extent necessary to conform"

-- (b)(2)(F) "At least 60 days prior to granting final approval of a project under this paragraph, the Secretary shall publish the
-- terms and conditions for any demonstration project conducted under the paragraph for public comment in the Federal Register and
-- shall notify the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and
-- Forestry of the Senate." A duty that runs before a later act cannot be a rule on the stable binary (`BEFORE` is rejected), so it
-- is a decision over days.
-- src:2461 | (F) At least 60 days prior to granting final approval of a project under this paragraph, the Secretary shall publish the terms and conditions for any demonstration project conducted under the paragraph for public comment in the Federal Register and shall notify the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate.
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(F) the Secretary's duty to publish and notify (src:2461)
`s 2026(b)(2)(F) the Secretary's duty to publish the terms and notify the Committees` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 publish the terms and conditions of a demonstration project and notify the Committees`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not publish the terms and conditions and notify the Committees at least 60 days before granting final approval"

-- src:2461 | (F) At least 60 days prior to granting final approval of a project under this paragraph, the Secretary shall publish the terms and conditions for any demonstration project conducted under the paragraph for public comment in the Federal Register and shall notify the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate.
@ref s 2026(b)(2)(F) at least 60 days prior to final approval (src:2461)
GIVEN `the Secretary has granted final approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms were published and both Committees notified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the publication and notice to the final approval, or to today if not yet approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(b)(2)(F) the Secretary published and notified at least 60 days before final approval` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the terms were published and both Committees notified` AND `days from the publication and notice to the final approval, or to today if not yet approved` AT LEAST 60 THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "At least 60 days prior to granting final approval of a project under this paragraph, the Secretary shall publish ... and shall notify"
        IF `the Secretary has granted final approval` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): final approval was granted without publication and notice at least 60 days earlier (a time bound read as a no, marginal reading)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): final approval has not been granted yet

