§§ `(c) Evaluation measures; pilot programs for nutritional monitoring`

-- (c) "The Secretary shall develop and implement measures for evaluating, on an annual or more frequent basis, the effectiveness
-- of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in achieving its stated objectives, including, but not limited to, the
-- program's impact upon the nutritional and economic status of participating households, the program's impact upon all sectors of
-- the agricultural economy, including farmers and ranchers, as well as retail food stores, and the program's relative fairness
-- to households of different income levels, different age composition, different size, and different regions of residence."
-- src:2466 | The Secretary shall develop and implement measures for evaluating, on an annual or more frequent basis, the effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in achieving its stated objectives, including, but not limited to, the program’s impact upon the nutritional and economic status of participating households, the program’s impact upon all sectors of the agricultural economy, including farmers and ranchers, as well as retail food stores, and the program’s relative fairness to households of different income levels, different age composition, different size, and different regions of residence. Further, the Secretary shall, by way of making contracts with or grants to public or private organizations or agencies, implement pilot programs to test various means of measuring on a continuing basis the nutritional status of low income people, with special emphasis on people who are eligible for supplemental nutrition assistance, in order to develop minimum common criteria and methods for systematic nutrition monitoring that could be applied on a nationwide basis. The locations of the pilot programs shall be selected to provide a representative geographic and demographic cross-section of political subdivisions that reflect natural usage patterns of health and nutritional services and that contain high proportions of low income people. The Secretary shall report on the progress of these pilot programs on an annual basis commencing on July 1, 1982, to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate, together with such recommendations as the Secretary deems appropriate.
@ref s 2026(c) the Secretary's duty to develop and implement evaluation measures (src:2466)
`s 2026(c) the Secretary's duty to develop and implement measures for evaluating the program` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 develop and implement measures for evaluating the program`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not develop and implement measures for evaluating the program"

-- src:2466 | The Secretary shall develop and implement measures for evaluating, on an annual or more frequent basis, the effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in achieving its stated objectives, including, but not limited to, the program’s impact upon the nutritional and economic status of participating households, the program’s impact upon all sectors of the agricultural economy, including farmers and ranchers, as well as retail food stores, and the program’s relative fairness to households of different income levels, different age composition, different size, and different regions of residence. Further, the Secretary shall, by way of making contracts with or grants to public or private organizations or agencies, implement pilot programs to test various means of measuring on a continuing basis the nutritional status of low income people, with special emphasis on people who are eligible for supplemental nutrition assistance, in order to develop minimum common criteria and methods for systematic nutrition monitoring that could be applied on a nationwide basis. The locations of the pilot programs shall be selected to provide a representative geographic and demographic cross-section of political subdivisions that reflect natural usage patterns of health and nutritional services and that contain high proportions of low income people. The Secretary shall report on the progress of these pilot programs on an annual basis commencing on July 1, 1982, to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate, together with such recommendations as the Secretary deems appropriate.
@ref s 2026(c) how often (src:2466)
GIVEN `the months between evaluations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(c) the evaluations are made often enough` MEANS
    IF `the months between evaluations` AT MOST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "on an annual or more frequent basis"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on an annual or more frequent basis"

DECLARE `s 2026 impact the measures cover` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 the program's impact upon the nutritional and economic status of participating households`
    `s 2026 the program's impact upon all sectors of the agricultural economy, including farmers and ranchers, as well as retail food stores`
    `s 2026 the program's relative fairness to households of different income levels, different age composition, different size, and different regions of residence`
    `s 2026 some other impact`

-- src:2466 | The Secretary shall develop and implement measures for evaluating, on an annual or more frequent basis, the effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in achieving its stated objectives, including, but not limited to, the program’s impact upon the nutritional and economic status of participating households, the program’s impact upon all sectors of the agricultural economy, including farmers and ranchers, as well as retail food stores, and the program’s relative fairness to households of different income levels, different age composition, different size, and different regions of residence. Further, the Secretary shall, by way of making contracts with or grants to public or private organizations or agencies, implement pilot programs to test various means of measuring on a continuing basis the nutritional status of low income people, with special emphasis on people who are eligible for supplemental nutrition assistance, in order to develop minimum common criteria and methods for systematic nutrition monitoring that could be applied on a nationwide basis. The locations of the pilot programs shall be selected to provide a representative geographic and demographic cross-section of political subdivisions that reflect natural usage patterns of health and nutritional services and that contain high proportions of low income people. The Secretary shall report on the progress of these pilot programs on an annual basis commencing on July 1, 1982, to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate, together with such recommendations as the Secretary deems appropriate.
@ref s 2026(c) what the measures cover (src:2466)
GIVEN impact IS A `s 2026 impact the measures cover`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(c) the measures shall cover the impact` MEANS
    CONSIDER impact
    WHEN `s 2026 some other impact` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including, but not limited to" leaves the list open
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "including, but not limited to, the program's impact upon ... the program's relative fairness"

