-- src:2466 | The Secretary shall develop and implement measures for evaluating, on an annual or more frequent basis, the effectiveness of the supplemental nutrition assistance program in achieving its stated objectives, including, but not limited to, the program’s impact upon the nutritional and economic status of participating households, the program’s impact upon all sectors of the agricultural economy, including farmers and ranchers, as well as retail food stores, and the program’s relative fairness to households of different income levels, different age composition, different size, and different regions of residence. Further, the Secretary shall, by way of making contracts with or grants to public or private organizations or agencies, implement pilot programs to test various means of measuring on a continuing basis the nutritional status of low income people, with special emphasis on people who are eligible for supplemental nutrition assistance, in order to develop minimum common criteria and methods for systematic nutrition monitoring that could be applied on a nationwide basis. The locations of the pilot programs shall be selected to provide a representative geographic and demographic cross-section of political subdivisions that reflect natural usage patterns of health and nutritional services and that contain high proportions of low income people. The Secretary shall report on the progress of these pilot programs on an annual basis commencing on July 1, 1982, to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate, together with such recommendations as the Secretary deems appropriate.
@ref s 2026(c) was the report on time (src:2466)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the date the Secretary submitted the report` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(c) the Secretary submitted the progress report for the year in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2026(c) the date by which the progress report for the year is due` year
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no report is due for that year
    WHEN JUST due THEN
        CONSIDER `the date the Secretary submitted the report`
        WHEN JUST submitted THEN
            IF submitted AT MOST due
            THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "on an annual basis commencing on July 1, 1982" is met
            ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the report was submitted after 1 July (a time bound read as a no, marginal reading)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF today GREATER THAN due
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): not submitted by 1 July (a time bound read as a no, marginal reading)
            ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet submitted and 1 July has not come

§§ `(d) Employment initiatives program`

-- (d)(1)(B) "A State shall be eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program under this subsection only if not less than
-- 50 percent of the households in the State that received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the summer of
-- 1993 also received benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act during the summer of 1993."
-- src:2472 | A State shall be eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program under this subsection only if not less than 50 percent of the households in the State that received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the summer of 1993 also received benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) during the summer of 1993.
@ref s 2026(d)(1)(B) the 50 percent requirement (src:2472)
GIVEN `the households in the State that received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the summer of 1993` IS A NUMBER
      `of those, the households that also received benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV during the summer of 1993` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(d)(1)(B) the State is eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program` MEANS
    IF 2 TIMES `of those, the households that also received benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV during the summer of 1993` AT LEAST `the households in the State that received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the summer of 1993`
    THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if" bars and grants nothing; the permission is in subparagraph (A)
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if not less than 50 percent of the households ... also received benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV"

-- (d)(1)(A) "Subject to the other provisions of this subsection, a State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program under this subsection."
-- src:2470 | Subject to the other provisions of this subsection, a State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program under this subsection.
@ref s 2026(d)(1)(A) election (src:2470)
-- (A) takes the two counts (B) takes and asks (B) itself, so that the NOTHING (B) gives when the 50 percent is met keeps one meaning:
-- "the bar is lifted and grants nothing", never "not supplied".
GIVEN `the households in the State that received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the summer of 1993` IS A NUMBER
      `of those, the households that also received benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV during the summer of 1993` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(d)(1)(A) the State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program` MEANS
    IF `s 2026(d)(1)(B) the State is eligible to carry out an employment initiatives program` `the households in the State that received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the summer of 1993` `of those, the households that also received benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV during the summer of 1993` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to the other provisions of this subsection", which includes the "only if" of subparagraph (B) (marginal reading (a))
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "a State may elect to carry out an employment initiatives program under this subsection"

-- (d)(3) "A household shall be eligible to receive cash benefits under paragraph (2) if an adult member of the household— (A) has
-- worked in unsubsidized employment for not less than the preceding 90 days; (B) has earned not less than $350 per month from the
-- employment referred to in subparagraph (A) for not less than the preceding 90 days; (C) (i) is receiving benefits under a State
-- program funded under part A of title IV ...; or (ii) was receiving benefits under such a program at the time the member first
-- received cash benefits under this subsection and is no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income; (D) is
-- continuing to earn not less than $350 per month from the employment referred to in subparagraph (A); and (E) elects to receive
-- cash benefits in lieu of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits under this subsection."
DECLARE `s 2026 adult member` HAS
    `the days the adult has worked in unsubsidized employment immediately before today`          IS A NUMBER
    `the least the adult earned in a month from that employment over those days, in dollars`    IS A NUMBER
    `the adult is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adult was receiving such benefits when first receiving cash benefits under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adult is no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adult is continuing to earn a month from that employment, in dollars`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the adult elects to receive cash benefits in lieu of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2487 | A household shall be eligible to receive cash benefits under paragraph (2) if an adult member of the household—
-- src:2488 | (A) has worked in unsubsidized employment for not less than the preceding 90 days;
-- src:2489 | (B) has earned not less than $350 per month from the employment referred to in subparagraph (A) for not less than the preceding 90 days;
-- src:2490 | (C)
-- src:2491 | (i) is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.); or
-- src:2492 | (ii) was receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) at the time the member first received cash benefits under this subsection and is no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income;
-- src:2493 | (D) is continuing to earn not less than $350 per month from the employment referred to in subparagraph (A); and
-- src:2494 | (E) elects to receive cash benefits in lieu of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits under this subsection.
@ref s 2026(d)(3) the adult member (src:2487-2494)
GIVEN adult IS A `s 2026 adult member`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(d)(3) the adult member meets subparagraphs (A) to (E)` MEANS
    IF adult's `the days the adult has worked in unsubsidized employment immediately before today` AT LEAST 90
       AND adult's `the least the adult earned in a month from that employment over those days, in dollars` AT LEAST 350
       AND (adult's `the adult is receiving benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV` OR (adult's `the adult was receiving such benefits when first receiving cash benefits under this subsection` AND adult's `the adult is no longer eligible for the State program because of earned income`))
       AND adult's `the adult is continuing to earn a month from that employment, in dollars` AT LEAST 350
       AND adult's `the adult elects to receive cash benefits in lieu of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(A) has worked ... not less than the preceding 90 days; (B) ... $350 per month ...; (C) ...; (D) ...; and (E) elects"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a failed "if an adult member of the household" meets (A) to (E) (marginal reading (a))

