    MUST `s 2026 conduct demonstration projects on vehicle exclusion limits`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not conduct a sufficient number of demonstration projects on vehicle exclusion limits"

-- src:2507 | The Secretary shall conduct a sufficient number of demonstration projects to evaluate the effects, in both rural and urban areas, of including in financial resources under section 2014(g) of this title the fair market value of licensed vehicles to the extent the value of each vehicle exceeds $4,500, but excluding the value of—
@ref s 2026(h) rural and urban areas (src:2507)
GIVEN `the demonstration projects evaluate the effects in rural areas` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demonstration projects evaluate the effects in urban areas` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(h) the demonstration projects evaluate the effects in both rural and urban areas` MEANS
    IF `the demonstration projects evaluate the effects in rural areas` AND `the demonstration projects evaluate the effects in urban areas`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "to evaluate the effects, in both rural and urban areas"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "a sufficient number" is not defined, and the text says nothing of what follows if one kind of area is missing

DECLARE `s 2026 vehicle` HAS
    `the fair market value of the licensed vehicle, in dollars`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `it is used to produce earned income`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is necessary for transportation of an elderly or physically disabled household member`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is used as the household's home`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is used to obtain, continue, or seek employment, including travel to and from work`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is used to pursue employment-related education or training`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is used to secure food or the benefits of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2507 | The Secretary shall conduct a sufficient number of demonstration projects to evaluate the effects, in both rural and urban areas, of including in financial resources under section 2014(g) of this title the fair market value of licensed vehicles to the extent the value of each vehicle exceeds $4,500, but excluding the value of—
@ref s 2026(h) the value over $4,500 (src:2507)
GIVEN vehicle IS A `s 2026 vehicle`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2026(h) the value of the vehicle over $4,500, in dollars` MEANS
    IF vehicle's `the fair market value of the licensed vehicle, in dollars` GREATER THAN 4500
    THEN vehicle's `the fair market value of the licensed vehicle, in dollars` MINUS 4500   -- "the fair market value of licensed vehicles to the extent the value of each vehicle exceeds $4,500"
    ELSE 0

-- src:2508 | (1) any licensed vehicle that is used to produce earned income, necessary for transportation of an elderly or physically disabled household member, or used as the household’s home; and
@ref s 2026(h)(1) vehicles excluded (src:2508)
GIVEN vehicle IS A `s 2026 vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2026(h)(1) the value of the vehicle is excluded` MEANS
    vehicle's `it is used to produce earned income` OR vehicle's `it is necessary for transportation of an elderly or physically disabled household member` OR vehicle's `it is used as the household's home`   -- "(1) any licensed vehicle that is used to produce earned income, necessary for transportation of an elderly or physically disabled household member, or used as the household's home"

-- the complement of (1), for the list filter below.
-- src:2508 | (1) any licensed vehicle that is used to produce earned income, necessary for transportation of an elderly or physically disabled household member, or used as the household’s home; and
@ref s 2026(h)(1) vehicles not excluded (src:2508)
GIVEN vehicle IS A `s 2026 vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2026(h)(1) the value of the vehicle is not excluded` MEANS
    NOT (`s 2026(h)(1) the value of the vehicle is excluded` vehicle)

-- src:2509 | (2) one licensed vehicle used to obtain, continue, or seek employment (including travel to and from work), used to pursue employment-related education or training, or used to secure food or the benefits of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2026(h)(2) the one vehicle that may be excluded (src:2509)
GIVEN vehicle IS A `s 2026 vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2026(h)(2) the vehicle is one of those from which one may be excluded` MEANS
    vehicle's `it is used to obtain, continue, or seek employment, including travel to and from work` OR vehicle's `it is used to pursue employment-related education or training` OR vehicle's `it is used to secure food or the benefits of the supplemental nutrition assistance program`   -- "(2) one licensed vehicle used to obtain, continue, or seek employment (including travel to and from work), used to pursue employment-related education or training, or used to secure food or the benefits"

-- Fork FR-26-3: when several vehicles qualify under (2), which one is excluded? Taken: the one whose value over $4,500 is the
-- greatest, so the household counts the least (the text says "one licensed vehicle" and does not choose).
-- src:2507 | The Secretary shall conduct a sufficient number of demonstration projects to evaluate the effects, in both rural and urban areas, of including in financial resources under section 2014(g) of this title the fair market value of licensed vehicles to the extent the value of each vehicle exceeds $4,500, but excluding the value of—
-- src:2508 | (1) any licensed vehicle that is used to produce earned income, necessary for transportation of an elderly or physically disabled household member, or used as the household’s home; and
-- src:2509 | (2) one licensed vehicle used to obtain, continue, or seek employment (including travel to and from work), used to pursue employment-related education or training, or used to secure food or the benefits of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2026(h) the value counted as financial resources (src:2507-2509)
GIVEN vehicles IS A LIST OF `s 2026 vehicle`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2026(h) the value of the vehicles counted as financial resources, in dollars` MEANS
    sum (map `s 2026(h) the value of the vehicle over $4,500, in dollars` rest) MINUS excludedUnderTwo   -- "the fair market value of licensed vehicles to the extent the value of each vehicle exceeds $4,500, but excluding the value of (1) ... and (2) one licensed vehicle"
    WHERE
        rest MEANS filter `s 2026(h)(1) the value of the vehicle is not excluded` vehicles
        candidates MEANS filter `s 2026(h)(2) the vehicle is one of those from which one may be excluded` rest
        excludedUnderTwo MEANS IF null candidates THEN 0 ELSE maximum (map `s 2026(h) the value of the vehicle over $4,500, in dollars` candidates)

§§ `(i) Testing resource accumulation`

-- (i) "The Secretary shall conduct, under such terms and conditions as the Secretary shall prescribe, for a period not to exceed 4
-- years, projects to test allowing not more than 11,000 eligible households, in the aggregate, to accumulate resources up to
-- $10,000 each (which shall be excluded from consideration as a resource) for later expenditure for a purpose directly related to
-- improving the education, training, or employability (including self-employment) of household members, for the purchase of a
-- home for the household, for a change of the household's residence, or for making major repairs to the household's home."
-- src:2511 | The Secretary shall conduct, under such terms and conditions as the Secretary shall prescribe, for a period not to exceed 4 years, projects to test allowing not more than 11,000 eligible households, in the aggregate, to accumulate resources up to $10,000 each (which shall be excluded from consideration as a resource) for later expenditure for a purpose directly related to improving the education, training, or employability (including self-employment) of household members, for the purchase of a home for the household, for a change of the household’s residence, or for making major repairs to the household’s home.
@ref s 2026(i) the Secretary's duty to conduct projects to test resource accumulation (src:2511)
`s 2026(i) the Secretary's duty to conduct projects to test resource accumulation` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 conduct projects to test resource accumulation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not conduct projects to test resource accumulation"

-- src:2511 | The Secretary shall conduct, under such terms and conditions as the Secretary shall prescribe, for a period not to exceed 4 years, projects to test allowing not more than 11,000 eligible households, in the aggregate, to accumulate resources up to $10,000 each (which shall be excluded from consideration as a resource) for later expenditure for a purpose directly related to improving the education, training, or employability (including self-employment) of household members, for the purchase of a home for the household, for a change of the household’s residence, or for making major repairs to the household’s home.
@ref s 2026(i) the period and the number of households (src:2511)
GIVEN `the years the projects run` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of eligible households, in the aggregate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(i) the projects are within the limits` MEANS
    IF `the years the projects run` AT MOST 4 AND `the number of eligible households, in the aggregate` AT MOST 11000
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "for a period not to exceed 4 years" and "not more than 11,000 eligible households, in the aggregate"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not to exceed 4 years" or "not more than 11,000 eligible households"

-- src:2511 | The Secretary shall conduct, under such terms and conditions as the Secretary shall prescribe, for a period not to exceed 4 years, projects to test allowing not more than 11,000 eligible households, in the aggregate, to accumulate resources up to $10,000 each (which shall be excluded from consideration as a resource) for later expenditure for a purpose directly related to improving the education, training, or employability (including self-employment) of household members, for the purchase of a home for the household, for a change of the household’s residence, or for making major repairs to the household’s home.
@ref s 2026(i) the resources excluded (src:2511)
GIVEN `the resources the household has accumulated for the purpose, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2026(i) the resources excluded from consideration as a resource, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the resources the household has accumulated for the purpose, in dollars` AT MOST 10000
    THEN `the resources the household has accumulated for the purpose, in dollars`   -- "accumulate resources up to $10,000 each (which shall be excluded from consideration as a resource)"
    ELSE 10000

DECLARE `s 2026 purpose of accumulated resources` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 improving the education, training, or employability, including self-employment, of household members`
    `s 2026 the purchase of a home for the household`
    `s 2026 a change of the household's residence`
    `s 2026 making major repairs to the household's home`
    `s 2026 some other purpose of expenditure`

-- src:2511 | The Secretary shall conduct, under such terms and conditions as the Secretary shall prescribe, for a period not to exceed 4 years, projects to test allowing not more than 11,000 eligible households, in the aggregate, to accumulate resources up to $10,000 each (which shall be excluded from consideration as a resource) for later expenditure for a purpose directly related to improving the education, training, or employability (including self-employment) of household members, for the purchase of a home for the household, for a change of the household’s residence, or for making major repairs to the household’s home.
@ref s 2026(i) the purpose of the later expenditure (src:2511)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 2026 purpose of accumulated resources`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(i) the purpose is one the projects test` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 2026 some other purpose of expenditure` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text does not say "only" or "nothing but"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "for later expenditure for a purpose directly related to improving the education, training, or employability ..., for the purchase of a home ..., for a change of the household's residence, or for making major repairs"

§§ `(j) Demonstration projects directed at benefit trafficking`

-- (j) "The Secretary shall use up to $4,000,000 of the funds provided in advance in appropriations Acts for projects authorized by
-- this section to conduct demonstration projects in which State or local supplemental nutrition assistance program agencies test
-- innovative ideas for working with State or local law enforcement agencies to investigate and prosecute benefit trafficking."
-- src:2513 | The Secretary shall use up to $4,000,000 of the funds provided in advance in appropriations Acts for projects authorized by this section to conduct demonstration projects in which State or local supplemental nutrition assistance program agencies test innovative ideas for working with State or local law enforcement agencies to investigate and prosecute benefit trafficking.
@ref s 2026(j) the Secretary's duty to use funds for demonstration projects directed at benefit trafficking (src:2513)
`s 2026(j) the Secretary's duty to use funds for demonstration projects directed at benefit trafficking` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 use funds for demonstration projects directed at benefit trafficking`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not use funds for demonstration projects directed at benefit trafficking"

-- src:2513 | The Secretary shall use up to $4,000,000 of the funds provided in advance in appropriations Acts for projects authorized by this section to conduct demonstration projects in which State or local supplemental nutrition assistance program agencies test innovative ideas for working with State or local law enforcement agencies to investigate and prosecute benefit trafficking.
@ref s 2026(j) up to $4,000,000 (src:2513)
GIVEN `the funds the Secretary uses, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(j) the funds used are within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the funds the Secretary uses, in dollars` AT MOST 4000000
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall use up to $4,000,000"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "up to $4,000,000"

§§ `(k) Pilot projects to evaluate health and nutrition promotion in the supplemental nutrition assistance program`

-- (k)(1) "The Secretary shall carry out, under such terms and conditions as the Secretary considers to be appropriate, pilot projects
-- to develop and test methods— (A) of using the supplemental nutrition assistance program to improve the dietary and health status
-- of households eligible for or participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and (B) to reduce overweight,
-- obesity (including childhood obesity), and associated co-morbidities in the United States."
-- src:2516 | The Secretary shall carry out, under such terms and conditions as the Secretary considers to be appropriate, pilot projects to develop and test methods—
@ref s 2026(k)(1) the Secretary's duty to carry out pilot projects (src:2516)
`s 2026(k)(1) the Secretary's duty to carry out pilot projects on health and nutrition promotion` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 carry out pilot projects on health and nutrition promotion`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not carry out pilot projects on health and nutrition promotion"

-- src:2517 | (A) of using the supplemental nutrition assistance program to improve the dietary and health status of households eligible for or participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:2518 | (B) to reduce overweight, obesity (including childhood obesity), and associated co-morbidities in the United States.
@ref s 2026(k)(1) the methods (src:2517-2518)
GIVEN `the pilot projects develop and test methods of using the supplemental nutrition assistance program to improve the dietary and health status of households` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pilot projects develop and test methods to reduce overweight, obesity, and associated co-morbidities in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(1) the pilot projects develop and test the methods the text requires` MEANS
    IF `the pilot projects develop and test methods of using the supplemental nutrition assistance program to improve the dietary and health status of households` AND `the pilot projects develop and test methods to reduce overweight, obesity, and associated co-morbidities in the United States`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "pilot projects to develop and test methods (A) of using the supplemental nutrition assistance program to improve the dietary and health status ...; and (B) to reduce overweight, obesity"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the pilot projects shall test and not what follows if they do not

-- (k)(2)(A) "In carrying out this subsection, the Secretary may enter into competitively awarded contracts or cooperative agreements
-- with, or provide grants to, public or private organizations or agencies (as defined by the Secretary), for use in accordance
-- with projects that meet the strategy goals of this subsection."
-- src:2521 | In carrying out this subsection, the Secretary may enter into competitively awarded contracts or cooperative agreements with, or provide grants to, public or private organizations or agencies (as defined by the Secretary), for use in accordance with projects that meet the strategy goals of this subsection.
@ref s 2026(k)(2)(A) contracts, cooperative agreements and grants (src:2521)
`s 2026(k)(2)(A) the Secretary's permission to enter into contracts or cooperative agreements or provide grants` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2026 enter into contracts or cooperative agreements, or provide grants, for the pilot projects`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (k)(2)(B) "To be eligible to receive a contract, cooperative agreement, or grant under this paragraph, an organization shall
-- submit to the Secretary an application at such time, in such manner, and containing such information as the Secretary may require."
-- src:2523 | To be eligible to receive a contract, cooperative agreement, or grant under this paragraph, an organization shall submit to the Secretary an application at such time, in such manner, and containing such information as the Secretary may require.
@ref s 2026(k)(2)(B) application (src:2523)
GIVEN `the organization has submitted an application at such time, in such manner, and containing such information as the Secretary requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(2)(B) the organization is eligible to receive a contract, cooperative agreement, or grant` MEANS
    IF `the organization has submitted an application at such time, in such manner, and containing such information as the Secretary requires`
    THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To be eligible ... an organization shall submit" states a necessary step and grants nothing
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To be eligible to receive a contract, cooperative agreement, or grant under this paragraph, an organization shall submit"

-- (k)(2)(C) "Pilot projects shall be evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria that may include— (i) identification of a
-- low-income target audience that corresponds to individuals living in households with incomes at or below 185 percent of the
-- poverty level; (ii) incorporation of a scientifically based strategy ...; (iii) a commitment to a pilot project that allows for a
-- rigorous outcome evaluation, including data collection; (iv) strategies to improve the nutritional value of food served during
-- school hours and during after-school hours; (v) innovative ways to provide significant improvement to the health and wellness of
-- children; (vi) other criteria, as determined by the Secretary."
DECLARE `s 2026 selection criterion` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 identification of a low-income target audience at or below 185 percent of the poverty level`
    `s 2026 incorporation of a scientifically based strategy designed to improve diet quality`
    `s 2026 a commitment to a pilot project that allows for a rigorous outcome evaluation, including data collection`
    `s 2026 strategies to improve the nutritional value of food served during school hours and after-school hours`
    `s 2026 innovative ways to provide significant improvement to the health and wellness of children`
    `s 2026 other criteria, as determined by the Secretary`
    `s 2026 a criterion not listed`

-- src:2525 | Pilot projects shall be evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria that may include—
-- src:2526 | (i) identification of a low-income target audience that corresponds to individuals living in households with incomes at or below 185 percent of the poverty level;
-- src:2527 | (ii) incorporation of a scientifically based strategy that is designed to improve diet quality through more healthful food purchases, preparation, or consumption;
-- src:2528 | (iii) a commitment to a pilot project that allows for a rigorous outcome evaluation, including data collection;
-- src:2529 | (iv) strategies to improve the nutritional value of food served during school hours and during after-school hours;
-- src:2530 | (v) innovative ways to provide significant improvement to the health and wellness of children;
-- src:2531 | (vi) other criteria, as determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2026(k)(2)(C) selection criteria (src:2525-2531)
GIVEN criterion IS A `s 2026 selection criterion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(2)(C) the criterion is one the pilot projects may be evaluated against` MEANS
    CONSIDER criterion
    WHEN `s 2026 a criterion not listed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): other criteria are "as determined by the Secretary"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "criteria that may include (i) ... (vi)"

-- src:2526 | (i) identification of a low-income target audience that corresponds to individuals living in households with incomes at or below 185 percent of the poverty level;
@ref s 2026(k)(2)(C)(i) the target audience (src:2526)
GIVEN `the household's income as a percent of the poverty level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(2)(C)(i) the individual is in the low-income target audience` MEANS
    IF `the household's income as a percent of the poverty level` AT MOST 185
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "individuals living in households with incomes at or below 185 percent of the poverty level"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the audience "corresponds to" those at or below 185 percent; the criteria "may include" it

-- src:2525 | Pilot projects shall be evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria that may include—
@ref s 2026(k)(2)(C) publicly disseminated (src:2525)
GIVEN `the criteria have been publicly disseminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(2)(C) the pilot projects are evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria` MEANS
    IF `the criteria have been publicly disseminated`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Pilot projects shall be evaluated against publicly disseminated criteria"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the pilot projects shall be evaluated against and not what follows if the criteria are not disseminated

-- (k)(2)(D) "Funds provided under this paragraph shall not be used for any project that limits the use of benefits under this chapter."
-- src:2533 | Funds provided under this paragraph shall not be used for any project that limits the use of benefits under this chapter.
@ref s 2026(k)(2)(D) use of funds (src:2533)
GIVEN `the project limits the use of benefits under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(2)(D) the funds may be used for the project` MEANS
    IF `the project limits the use of benefits under this chapter`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Funds provided under this paragraph shall not be used for any project that limits the use of benefits under this chapter"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not be used" bars and grants nothing

-- (k)(3) "Pilot projects carried out under paragraph (1) may include projects to determine whether healthier food purchases by and
-- healthier diets among households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program result from projects that— (A)
-- increase the supplemental nutrition assistance purchasing power ...; (B) increase access to farmers' markets ...; (C) provide
-- incentives to authorized supplemental nutrition assistance program retailers ...; (D) subject authorized ... retailers to
-- stricter retailer requirements ...; (E) provide incentives at the point of purchase ...; or (F) provide to participating
-- households integrated communication and education programs ..."
DECLARE `s 2026 kind of pilot project` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 increase the supplemental nutrition assistance purchasing power of the participating households`
    `s 2026 increase access to farmers' markets through the electronic redemption of benefits`
    `s 2026 provide incentives to authorized retailers to increase the availability of healthy foods`
    `s 2026 subject authorized retailers to stricter requirements with respect to carrying and stocking healthful foods`
    `s 2026 provide incentives at the point of purchase to purchase fruits, vegetables, or other healthful foods`
    `s 2026 provide integrated communication and education programs`
    `s 2026 some other kind of project`

-- src:2535 | Pilot projects carried out under paragraph (1) may include projects to determine whether healthier food purchases by and healthier diets among households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program result from projects that—
-- src:2536 | (A) increase the supplemental nutrition assistance purchasing power of the participating households by providing increased supplemental nutrition assistance program benefit allotments to the participating households;
-- src:2537 | (B) increase access to farmers [Footnote: 2 So in original. Probably should be “farmers’ ”.] markets by participating households through the electronic redemption of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits at farmers’ markets;
-- src:2538 | (C) provide incentives to authorized supplemental nutrition assistance program retailers to increase the availability of healthy foods to participating households;
-- src:2539 | (D) subject authorized supplemental nutrition assistance program retailers to stricter retailer requirements with respect to carrying and stocking healthful foods;
-- src:2540 | (E) provide incentives at the point of purchase to encourage households participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program to purchase fruits, vegetables, or other healthful foods; or
-- src:2541 | (F) provide to participating households integrated communication and education programs, including the provision of funding for a portion of a school-based nutrition coordinator to implement a broad nutrition action plan and parent nutrition education programs in elementary schools, separately or in combination with pilot projects carried out under subparagraphs (A) through (E).
@ref s 2026(k)(3) projects (src:2535-2541)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 2026 kind of pilot project`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(3) the pilot projects may include projects of this kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 2026 some other kind of project` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may include" does not say "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may include projects ... that (A) ...; (B) ...; (C) ...; (D) ...; (E) ...; or (F)"

-- (k)(4)(A)(i) "The Secretary shall provide for an independent evaluation of projects selected under this subsection that measures the
-- impact of the pilot program on health and nutrition as described in paragraph (1). The independent evaluation under subclause
-- (I) shall use rigorous methodologies, particularly random assignment or other methods that are capable of producing
-- scientifically valid information regarding which activities are effective."
-- src:2546 | The Secretary shall provide for an independent evaluation of projects selected under this subsection that measures the impact of the pilot program on health and nutrition as described in paragraph (1).
@ref s 2026(k)(4)(A)(i)(I) the Secretary's duty to provide for an independent evaluation (src:2546)
`s 2026(k)(4)(A)(i)(I) the Secretary's duty to provide for an independent evaluation` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 provide for an independent evaluation of the pilot projects`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not provide for an independent evaluation of the projects selected"

-- src:2548 | The independent evaluation under subclause (I) shall use rigorous methodologies, particularly random assignment or other methods that are capable of producing scientifically valid information regarding which activities are effective.
@ref s 2026(k)(4)(A)(i)(II) rigorous methodologies (src:2548)
GIVEN `the independent evaluation uses rigorous methodologies, particularly random assignment or other methods capable of producing scientifically valid information regarding which activities are effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(4)(A)(i)(II) the independent evaluation uses the methodologies the text requires` MEANS
    IF `the independent evaluation uses rigorous methodologies, particularly random assignment or other methods capable of producing scientifically valid information regarding which activities are effective`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall use rigorous methodologies, particularly random assignment or other methods that are capable of producing scientifically valid information"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the evaluation shall use and not what follows if it does not

-- (k)(4)(A)(ii) "The Secretary may use funds provided to carry out this section to pay costs associated with monitoring and
-- evaluating each pilot project."
-- src:2550 | The Secretary may use funds provided to carry out this section to pay costs associated with monitoring and evaluating each pilot project.
@ref s 2026(k)(4)(A)(ii) costs (src:2550)
`s 2026(k)(4)(A)(ii) the Secretary's permission to pay the costs of monitoring and evaluating a pilot project` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2026 pay the costs of monitoring and evaluating a pilot project`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (k)(4)(B) "Not later than 90 days after the last day of fiscal year 2009 and each fiscal year thereafter until the completion of
-- the last evaluation under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of
-- Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that includes a description of—
-- (i) the status of each pilot project; (ii) the results of the evaluation completed during the previous fiscal year; and (iii)
-- to the maximum extent practicable— (I) the impact ...; (II) baseline information ...; and (III) equivalent information about
-- similar or identical measures among control or comparison groups."
-- Fork FR-26-4: "until the completion of the last evaluation": a report is due for each fiscal year up to and including the one
-- in which the last evaluation is completed. The fiscal year ends on 30 September.
-- src:2552 | Not later than 90 days after the last day of fiscal year 2009 and each fiscal year thereafter until the completion of the last evaluation under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that includes a description of—
@ref s 2026(k)(4)(B) the Secretary's duty to submit the report (src:2552)
`s 2026(k)(4)(B) the Secretary's duty to submit the report on the pilot projects` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 submit the report on the pilot projects to the Committees`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not submit the report on the pilot projects to the Committees"

-- src:2552 | Not later than 90 days after the last day of fiscal year 2009 and each fiscal year thereafter until the completion of the last evaluation under subparagraph (A), the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report that includes a description of—
@ref s 2026(k)(4)(B) the date by which the report for the fiscal year is due (src:2552)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the fiscal year in which the last evaluation under subparagraph (A) is completed, if it is` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2026(k)(4)(B) the date by which the report for the fiscal year is due` MEANS
    IF `fiscal year` LESS THAN 2009
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the last day of fiscal year 2009 and each fiscal year thereafter"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the fiscal year in which the last evaluation under subparagraph (A) is completed, if it is`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (Date (Day (Date 30 9 `fiscal year`) PLUS 90))   -- "Not later than 90 days after the last day of" the fiscal year
         WHEN JUST last THEN
             IF `fiscal year` AT MOST last
             THEN JUST (Date (Day (Date 30 9 `fiscal year`) PLUS 90))   -- "until the completion of the last evaluation" (fork FR-26-4)
             ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "until the completion of the last evaluation"

-- the report's contents, as a record:
DECLARE `s 2026 pilot project report` HAS
    `a description of the status of each pilot project`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a description of the results of the evaluation completed during the previous fiscal year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the impact of the pilot project on health, nutrition, and associated behavioral outcomes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `baseline information relevant to the stated goals and desired outcomes`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `equivalent information about control or comparison groups`                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2553 | (i) the status of each pilot project;
-- src:2554 | (ii) the results of the evaluation completed during the previous fiscal year; and
-- src:2555 | (iii) to the maximum extent practicable—
-- src:2556 | (I) the impact of the pilot project on appropriate health, nutrition, and associated behavioral outcomes among households participating in the pilot project;
-- src:2557 | (II) baseline information relevant to the stated goals and desired outcomes of the pilot project; and
-- src:2558 | (III) equivalent information about similar or identical measures among control or comparison groups that did not participate in the pilot project.
@ref s 2026(k)(4)(B) contents (src:2553-2558)
GIVEN report IS A `s 2026 pilot project report`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(4)(B) the report includes what the text requires` MEANS
    IF report's `a description of the status of each pilot project`
       AND report's `a description of the results of the evaluation completed during the previous fiscal year`
       AND report's `the impact of the pilot project on health, nutrition, and associated behavioral outcomes`
       AND report's `baseline information relevant to the stated goals and desired outcomes`
       AND report's `equivalent information about control or comparison groups`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "a report that includes a description of (i) the status of each pilot project; (ii) the results ...; and (iii) to the maximum extent practicable (I) ...; (II) ...; and (III) ..."
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (iii) is "to the maximum extent practicable", and for (i) and (ii) the text says nothing of what follows if one is missing

-- (k)(4)(C) "In addition to the reporting requirements under subparagraph (B), evaluation results shall be shared broadly to inform
-- policy makers, service providers, other partners, and the public in order to promote wide use of successful strategies."
-- src:2560 | In addition to the reporting requirements under subparagraph (B), evaluation results shall be shared broadly to inform policy makers, service providers, other partners, and the public in order to promote wide use of successful strategies.
@ref s 2026(k)(4)(C) public dissemination (src:2560)
`s 2026(k)(4)(C) the Secretary's duty to share the evaluation results broadly` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 share the evaluation results broadly`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not share the evaluation results broadly"

-- (k)(5)(A) "There are authorized to be appropriated such sums as are necessary to carry out this section for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2012."
-- src:2563 | There are authorized to be appropriated such sums as are necessary to carry out this section for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2012.
@ref s 2026(k)(5)(A) authorization of appropriations (src:2563)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(k)(5)(A) sums are authorized to be appropriated for the fiscal year` MEANS
    IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2008 AND `fiscal year` AT MOST 2012
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "such sums as are necessary to carry out this section for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2012"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for each of fiscal years 2008 through 2012"

-- (k)(5)(B) "Out of any funds made available under section 2027 of this title, on October 1, 2008, the Secretary shall make available
-- $20,000,000 to carry out a project described in paragraph (3)(E), to remain available until expended."
-- src:2565 | Out of any funds made available under section 2027 of this title, on October 1, 2008, the Secretary shall make available $20,000,000 to carry out a project described in paragraph (3)(E), to remain available until expended.
@ref s 2026(k)(5)(B) mandatory funding (src:2565)
`s 2026(k)(5)(B) the Secretary's duty to make available the mandatory funding` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 make available the mandatory funding for the pilot project`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not make available $20,000,000 to carry out a project described in paragraph (3)(E)"

-- src:2565 | Out of any funds made available under section 2027 of this title, on October 1, 2008, the Secretary shall make available $20,000,000 to carry out a project described in paragraph (3)(E), to remain available until expended.
@ref s 2026(k)(5)(B) the amount (src:2565)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2026(k)(5)(B) the amount the Secretary shall make available on the day, in dollars` MEANS
    IF day EQUALS (Date 1 10 2008)
    THEN JUST 20000000   -- "on October 1, 2008, the Secretary shall make available $20,000,000"
    ELSE NOTHING         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on October 1, 2008"

§§ `(l) Cooperation with program research and evaluation`

-- (l) "Subject to the requirements of this chapter, including protections under section 2020(e)(8) of this title, States, State
-- agencies, local agencies, institutions, facilities such as data consortiums, and contractors participating in programs
-- authorized under this chapter shall— (1) cooperate with officials and contractors acting on behalf of the Secretary in the
-- conduct of evaluations and studies under this chapter; and (2) submit information at such time and in such manner as the
-- Secretary may require."
DECLARE `s 2026 participant` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 a State`
    `s 2026 a State agency`
    `s 2026 a local agency`
    `s 2026 an institution`
    `s 2026 a facility such as a data consortium`
    `s 2026 a contractor`
    `s 2026 someone else`

-- src:2567 | Subject to the requirements of this chapter, including protections under section 2020(e)(8) of this title, States, State agencies, local agencies, institutions, facilities such as data consortiums, and contractors participating in programs authorized under this chapter shall—
@ref s 2026(l) who shall cooperate (src:2567)
GIVEN participant IS A `s 2026 participant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(l) the participant shall cooperate and submit information` MEANS
    CONSIDER participant
    WHEN `s 2026 someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "States, State agencies, local agencies, institutions, facilities such as data consortiums, and contractors participating in programs authorized under this chapter"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "States, State agencies, local agencies, institutions, facilities such as data consortiums, and contractors ... shall"

-- src:2568 | (1) cooperate with officials and contractors acting on behalf of the Secretary in the conduct of evaluations and studies under this chapter; and
@ref s 2026(l)(1) the State agency's duty to cooperate (src:2568)
`s 2026(l)(1) the State agency's duty to cooperate with the Secretary's officials and contractors` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2026 cooperate with officials and contractors acting on behalf of the Secretary`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency did not cooperate with officials and contractors acting on behalf of the Secretary in the conduct of evaluations and studies"

-- src:2569 | (2) submit information at such time and in such manner as the Secretary may require.
@ref s 2026(l)(2) the State agency's duty to submit information (src:2569)
`s 2026(l)(2) the State agency's duty to submit information` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2026 submit information to the Secretary`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency did not submit information at the time and in the manner the Secretary required"

-- src:2567 | Subject to the requirements of this chapter, including protections under section 2020(e)(8) of this title, States, State agencies, local agencies, institutions, facilities such as data consortiums, and contractors participating in programs authorized under this chapter shall—
@ref s 2026(l) subject to the protections of section 2020(e)(8) (src:2567)
GIVEN `s 2020(e)(8) the information is protected from disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(l) the participant shall submit the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2020(e)(8) the information is protected from disclosure`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall submit information at such time and in such manner as the Secretary may require"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to the requirements of this chapter, including protections under section 2020(e)(8)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 2020(e)(8) protects the information is that section's answer

§§ `(m) Evaluation of child support enforcement cooperation requirements`

-- (m)(1) "The Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of Health and Human Services, shall conduct an independent evaluation of
-- a representative sample of States— (A) to assess the implementation and impact of the eligibility requirements described in
-- subsections (l) through (n) of section 2015 ...; (B) to assess the factors that contributed to the decision of States that
-- formerly implemented the eligibility requirements ... to cease such implementation; (C) to review alternatives ...; and (D) to
-- evaluate the costs and benefits to households and to State agencies, of requiring State agencies to implement each of the
-- eligibility requirements described in subsections (l) through (n) of section 2015."
-- src:2572 | The Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of Health and Human Services, shall conduct an independent evaluation of a representative sample of States—
@ref s 2026(m)(1) the Secretary's duty to conduct the evaluation (src:2572)
`s 2026(m)(1) the Secretary's duty to conduct an independent evaluation of the child support cooperation requirements` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 conduct an independent evaluation of the child support cooperation requirements`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not conduct an independent evaluation of a representative sample of States"

DECLARE `s 2026 evaluation of child support cooperation` HAS
    `the Secretary consulted the Secretary of Health and Human Services`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evaluation is independent and covers a representative sample of States`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it assesses the implementation and impact of the eligibility requirements and the feasibility of implementing them in other States` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it assesses the factors that contributed to the decision of States to cease implementation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it reviews alternatives used by other States and their effectiveness`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `it evaluates the costs and benefits to households and to State agencies`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2572 | The Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of Health and Human Services, shall conduct an independent evaluation of a representative sample of States—
-- src:2573 | (A) to assess the implementation and impact of the eligibility requirements described in subsections (l) through (n) of section 2015 of this title in States that have formerly implemented or continue to implement those requirements, and the feasibility of implementing those requirements in other States;
-- src:2574 | (B) to assess the factors that contributed to the decision of States that formerly implemented the eligibility requirements described in each of subsections (l) through (n) of section 2015 of this title to cease such implementation;
-- src:2575 | (C) to review alternatives to the eligibility requirements described in each of subsections (l) through (n) of section 2015 of this title that are used by other States to assist participants in the supplemental nutrition assistance program to make or receive child support payments and the effectiveness of those alternatives; and
-- src:2576 | (D) to evaluate the costs and benefits to households and to State agencies, of requiring State agencies to implement each of the eligibility requirements described in subsections (l) through (n) of section 2015 of this title.
@ref s 2026(m)(1) the evaluation (src:2572-2576)
GIVEN evaluation IS A `s 2026 evaluation of child support cooperation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(m)(1) the evaluation is as the text requires` MEANS
    IF evaluation's `the Secretary consulted the Secretary of Health and Human Services`
       AND evaluation's `the evaluation is independent and covers a representative sample of States`
       AND evaluation's `it assesses the implementation and impact of the eligibility requirements and the feasibility of implementing them in other States`
       AND evaluation's `it assesses the factors that contributed to the decision of States to cease implementation`
       AND evaluation's `it reviews alternatives used by other States and their effectiveness`
       AND evaluation's `it evaluates the costs and benefits to households and to State agencies`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The Secretary, in consultation with the Secretary of Health and Human Services, shall conduct an independent evaluation of a representative sample of States (A) to assess ...; (B) ...; (C) ...; and (D)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the evaluation shall be and not what follows if it is not

-- (m)(2) "The evaluation under paragraph (1) shall include, to the maximum extent practicable, an assessment of— (A) the manner in
-- which applicable State agencies implement and enforce the eligibility requirements ...; (B) the Federal, State, and local costs
-- ...; (C) the effect of those eligibility requirements on the establishment of new child support orders, ...; (D) ... (i) the number
-- of individuals subject to those requirements; (ii) the number ... who meet those requirements; and (iii) the number ... who
-- fail to meet them; (E) the number of individuals in each State for whom good cause for noncooperation has been found under
-- section 2015(l)(2); (F) the impact of those eligibility requirements on the supplemental nutrition assistance program
-- eligibility, benefit levels, food security, income, and economic stability of— (i) individuals subject to those requirements;
-- (ii) the household members of those individuals, including children; and (iii) households with nontraditional family structures."
DECLARE `s 2026 assessment` HAS
    `(A) the manner in which State agencies implement and enforce the requirements, including the procedures and their alignment with other Federal programs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(B) the Federal, State, and local costs of implementing the requirements`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `(C) the effect of the requirements on child support orders, paternity, payments and arrears` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(D) the number of individuals subject to the requirements, who meet them, and who fail to meet them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(E) the number of individuals for whom good cause for noncooperation has been found`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `(F) the impact of the requirements on eligibility, benefit levels, food security, income, and economic stability of the three groups` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2578 | The evaluation under paragraph (1) shall include, to the maximum extent practicable, an assessment of—
-- src:2579 | (A) the manner in which applicable State agencies implement and enforce the eligibility requirements described in subparagraph (A) of such paragraph, including—
-- src:2580 | (i) the procedures used by each State to determine cooperation, to sanction participants for failure to cooperate, and to determine good cause for noncooperation under each of subsections (l) through (n) of section 2015 of this title; and
-- src:2581 | (ii) the manner in which each State aligns the procedures for implementing those eligibility requirements with procedures for implementing other Federal programs that require cooperation with child support enforcement, including the program of block grants to States for temporary assistance for needy families established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), the Medicaid program under title XIX of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1396 et seq.), and programs carried out under the Child Care and Development Block Grant Act of 1990 (42 U.S.C. 9857 et seq.);
-- src:2582 | (B) the Federal, State, and local costs associated with implementing those eligibility requirements, including costs incurred under this chapter and by child support enforcement agencies for personnel, technology upgrades, and other costs;
-- src:2583 | (C) the effect of those eligibility requirements on the establishment of new child support orders, the establishment of paternity, changes in child support payments to custodial households, and changes in arrears owed on child support orders;
-- src:2584 | (D) with respect to the eligibility requirements under each of subsections (l) through (n) of section 2015 of this title—
-- src:2585 | (i) the number of individuals subject to those requirements;
-- src:2586 | (ii) the number of individuals in each State who meet those requirements; and
-- src:2587 | (iii) the number of individuals in each State who fail to meet those requirements;
-- src:2588 | (E) the number of individuals in each State for whom good cause for noncooperation has been found under section 2015(l)(2) of this title;
-- src:2589 | (F) the impact of those eligibility requirements on the supplemental nutrition assistance program eligibility, benefit levels, food security, income, and economic stability of—
-- src:2590 | (i) individuals subject to those requirements;
-- src:2591 | (ii) the household members of those individuals, including children; and
-- src:2592 | (iii) households with nontraditional family structures, including a household in which a grandparent is the primary caretaker of a grandchild of the grandparent.
@ref s 2026(m)(2) the assessment (src:2578-2592)
GIVEN assessment IS A `s 2026 assessment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(m)(2) the evaluation includes the assessment the text requires` MEANS
    IF assessment's `(A) the manner in which State agencies implement and enforce the requirements, including the procedures and their alignment with other Federal programs`
       AND assessment's `(B) the Federal, State, and local costs of implementing the requirements`
       AND assessment's `(C) the effect of the requirements on child support orders, paternity, payments and arrears`
       AND assessment's `(D) the number of individuals subject to the requirements, who meet them, and who fail to meet them`
       AND assessment's `(E) the number of individuals for whom good cause for noncooperation has been found`
       AND assessment's `(F) the impact of the requirements on eligibility, benefit levels, food security, income, and economic stability of the three groups`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The evaluation under paragraph (1) shall include ... an assessment of (A) ...; (F)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the maximum extent practicable"

-- (m)(3) "Each State agency selected under paragraph (1) shall provide information to the Secretary necessary to conduct the
-- evaluation under such paragraph."
-- src:2594 | Each State agency selected under paragraph (1) shall provide information to the Secretary necessary to conduct the evaluation under such paragraph.
@ref s 2026(m)(3) the State agency's duty to provide information (src:2594)
`s 2026(m)(3) the State agency's duty to provide information for the evaluation` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2026 provide information to the Secretary for the evaluation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency selected under paragraph (1) did not provide information to the Secretary necessary to conduct the evaluation"

-- (m)(4) "Not later than 3 years after December 20, 2018, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House
-- of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report describing the findings from
-- the evaluation conducted under paragraph (1)."
-- src:2596 | Not later than 3 years after December 20, 2018, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report describing the findings from the evaluation conducted under paragraph (1).
@ref s 2026(m)(4) the Secretary's duty to report (src:2596)
`s 2026(m)(4) the Secretary's duty to report on the evaluation` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 submit the report on the evaluation of child support cooperation to the Committees`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not report the findings of the evaluation to the Committees"

-- src:2596 | Not later than 3 years after December 20, 2018, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report describing the findings from the evaluation conducted under paragraph (1).
@ref s 2026(m)(4) the date by which the report is due (src:2596)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2026(m)(4) the date by which the report is due` MEANS
    Date 20 12 2021   -- "Not later than 3 years after December 20, 2018"

-- src:2596 | Not later than 3 years after December 20, 2018, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report describing the findings from the evaluation conducted under paragraph (1).
@ref s 2026(m)(4) was the report on time (src:2596)
GIVEN `the date the Secretary submitted the report` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(m)(4) the Secretary submitted the report in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the Secretary submitted the report`
    WHEN JUST submitted THEN
        IF submitted AT MOST `s 2026(m)(4) the date by which the report is due`
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Not later than 3 years after December 20, 2018"
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 3 years after December 20, 2018" (a time bound read as a no, marginal reading)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF today GREATER THAN `s 2026(m)(4) the date by which the report is due`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): not submitted by 20 December 2021 (a time bound read as a no, marginal reading)
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet submitted and the date has not come

§§ `(n) Longitudinal data for research`

-- (n)(1) "Subject to paragraphs (3) through (5), a State agency may, on approval by the Secretary, establish a longitudinal database
-- that contains information about households and members of households that receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition
-- assistance program in the State."
-- src:2599 | Subject to paragraphs (3) through (5), a State agency may, on approval by the Secretary, establish a longitudinal database that contains information about households and members of households that receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the State.
@ref s 2026(n)(1) the State agency's permission to establish a longitudinal database (src:2599)
`s 2026(n)(1) the State agency's permission to establish a longitudinal database` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MAY `s 2026 establish a longitudinal database`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:2599 | Subject to paragraphs (3) through (5), a State agency may, on approval by the Secretary, establish a longitudinal database that contains information about households and members of households that receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the State.
@ref s 2026(n)(1) on approval (src:2599)
GIVEN `the Secretary has approved the establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(1) the State agency may establish a longitudinal database` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary has approved the establishment`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "a State agency may, on approval by the Secretary, establish a longitudinal database"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on approval by the Secretary", as "Subject to the approval of the Secretary" is read in s 2036a(c)(5) (marginal reading (b))

-- (n)(2) "Each longitudinal database established under paragraph (1) shall be used solely to conduct research on participation in and
-- the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including duration of participation in the program."
DECLARE `s 2026 use of the database` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 research on participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including duration of participation`
    `s 2026 research on the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
    `s 2026 some other use`

-- src:2601 | Each longitudinal database established under paragraph (1) shall be used solely to conduct research on participation in and the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including duration of participation in the program.
@ref s 2026(n)(2) purpose (src:2601)
GIVEN use IS A `s 2026 use of the database`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(2) the database may be used this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    WHEN `s 2026 some other use` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be used solely to conduct research on participation in and the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "research on participation in and the operation of the supplemental nutrition assistance program, including duration of participation"

-- (n)(3) "Prior to the approval of State agencies to establish longitudinal databases under paragraph (1), the Secretary shall— (A)
-- identify features that shall be standard across States ...; (B) identify features ... that may vary across States; (C) identify
-- a procedure for States ... to use a unique identifier ...; (D) establish the manner in which data security and privacy
-- protections ... shall be implemented and maintained; (E) provide direction to State agencies on the responsibilities of and
-- funding arrangements ...; (F) provide a description of the documentation that States shall submit to the Secretary prior to
-- allowing researchers access ...; (G) consult with other Federal research agencies, including the Bureau of the Census; (H)
-- consult with States that have already established databases ...; and (I) identify any other requirements determined appropriate
-- by the Secretary."
-- src:2603 | Prior to the approval of State agencies to establish longitudinal databases under paragraph (1), the Secretary shall—
@ref s 2026(n)(3) the Secretary's duty to complete the preparations (src:2603)
`s 2026(n)(3) the Secretary's duty to complete the preparations before approving longitudinal databases` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 complete the preparations before approving longitudinal databases`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary approved State agencies to establish longitudinal databases before completing the preparations in paragraph (3)"

DECLARE `s 2026 preparations` HAS
    `(A) the features that shall be standard across States are identified`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `(B) the features that may vary across States are identified`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `(C) a procedure for a unique identifier is identified`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `(D) the manner in which data security and privacy protections are implemented and maintained is established` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(E) direction on responsibilities and funding arrangements is provided`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `(F) a description of the documentation States submit before allowing researchers access is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(G) other Federal research agencies, including the Bureau of the Census, are consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(H) States that have already established databases are consulted`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `(I) any other requirements determined appropriate are identified`                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2604 | (A) identify features that shall be standard across States such as database format to facilitate use of longitudinal databases established under paragraph (1) for research purposes;
-- src:2605 | (B) identify features of longitudinal databases established under paragraph (1) that may vary across States;
-- src:2606 | (C) identify a procedure for States operating longitudinal databases under paragraph (1) to use a unique identifier to provide relevant information on household members who receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program for the purpose of comparing participation data in multiple participating States over time while protecting participant privacy;
-- src:2607 | (D) establish the manner in which data security and privacy protections, as required by Federal law and consistent with other appropriate practices, shall be implemented and maintained;
-- src:2608 | (E) provide direction to State agencies on the responsibilities of and funding arrangements for State agencies and any State contractors (including entities providing technical assistance) relating to the establishment and operation of a longitudinal database;
-- src:2609 | (F) provide a description of the documentation that States shall submit to the Secretary prior to allowing researchers access to a longitudinal database;
-- src:2610 | (G) consult with other Federal research agencies, including the Bureau of the Census;
-- src:2611 | (H) consult with States that have already established databases used for purposes similar to the purposes outlined in this subsection; and
-- src:2612 | (I) identify any other requirements determined appropriate by the Secretary.
@ref s 2026(n)(3) prior to approval (src:2604-2612)
GIVEN preparations IS A `s 2026 preparations`
      `the Secretary has approved State agencies to establish longitudinal databases` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(3) the Secretary has completed the preparations the text requires` MEANS
    IF preparations's `(A) the features that shall be standard across States are identified`
       AND preparations's `(B) the features that may vary across States are identified`
       AND preparations's `(C) a procedure for a unique identifier is identified`
       AND preparations's `(D) the manner in which data security and privacy protections are implemented and maintained is established`
       AND preparations's `(E) direction on responsibilities and funding arrangements is provided`
       AND preparations's `(F) a description of the documentation States submit before allowing researchers access is provided`
       AND preparations's `(G) other Federal research agencies, including the Bureau of the Census, are consulted`
       AND preparations's `(H) States that have already established databases are consulted`
       AND preparations's `(I) any other requirements determined appropriate are identified`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Prior to the approval of State agencies ..., the Secretary shall (A) ...; (I)"
    ELSE IF `the Secretary has approved State agencies to establish longitudinal databases`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Prior to the approval of State agencies to establish longitudinal databases under paragraph (1), the Secretary shall" complete (A) to (I)
         ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no approval has been given yet and the preparations are not all complete

-- (n)(4)(A) "Subject to subparagraph (B), each longitudinal database established under paragraph (1)— (i) shall include monthly
-- information about households and members of households that receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance
-- program in the participating State taken from existing information collected by the State agency including, if available,— (I)
-- demographic characteristics; (II) income and financial resources (as described in section 2014(g)); (III) employment status;
-- (IV) household circumstances, such as deductible expenses; and (V) the amount of the monthly allotment received; and (ii) may
-- include information from other State data sources such as— (I) earnings and employment data from the State department of labor;
-- (II) health insurance program data; or (III) data from participation in other programs administered by the State."
DECLARE `s 2026 kind of data` IS ONE OF
    `s 2026 demographic characteristics`
    `s 2026 income and financial resources`
    `s 2026 employment status`
    `s 2026 household circumstances, such as deductible expenses`
    `s 2026 the amount of the monthly allotment received`
    `s 2026 earnings and employment data from the State department of labor`
    `s 2026 health insurance program data`
    `s 2026 data from participation in other programs administered by the State`
    `s 2026 some other data`

-- src:2615 | Subject to subparagraph (B), each longitudinal database established under paragraph (1)—
-- src:2616 | (i) shall include monthly information about households and members of households that receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in the participating State taken from existing information collected by the State agency including, if available,—
-- src:2617 | (I) demographic characteristics;
-- src:2618 | (II) income and financial resources (as described in section 2014(g) of this title);
-- src:2619 | (III) employment status;
-- src:2620 | (IV) household circumstances, such as deductible expenses; and
-- src:2621 | (V) the amount of the monthly allotment received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- src:2622 | (ii) may include information from other State data sources such as—
-- src:2623 | (I) earnings and employment data from the State department of labor;
-- src:2624 | (II) health insurance program data; or
-- src:2625 | (III) data from participation in other programs administered by the State.
@ref s 2026(n)(4)(A) included data (src:2615-2625)
GIVEN data IS A `s 2026 kind of data`
      `the information is available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(4)(A) the database includes the data` MEANS
    CONSIDER data
    WHEN `s 2026 some other data` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "such as" and "including" leave the lists open
    WHEN `s 2026 earnings and employment data from the State department of labor` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(ii) may include information from other State data sources such as (I) earnings and employment data from the State department of labor"
    WHEN `s 2026 health insurance program data` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(II) health insurance program data"
    WHEN `s 2026 data from participation in other programs administered by the State` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(III) data from participation in other programs administered by the State"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the information is available`
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "(i) shall include monthly information ... including, if available, (I) demographic characteristics; ... (V) the amount of the monthly allotment"
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if available"

-- (n)(4)(B) "Any State that establishes a longitudinal database under paragraph (1) shall, in accordance with all applicable Federal
-- and State privacy standards and requirements— (i) protect the privacy of information about each member of each household that
-- receives benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in such State by ensuring that no personally identifiable
-- information (including social security number, home address, or contact information) is included in the longitudinal database;
-- and (ii) make the data under this paragraph available to researchers and the Secretary."
-- src:2628 | (i) protect the privacy of information about each member of each household that receives benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in such State by ensuring that no personally identifiable information (including social security number, home address, or contact information) is included in the longitudinal database; and
@ref s 2026(n)(4)(B)(i) the State agency's duty to protect privacy (src:2628)
`s 2026(n)(4)(B)(i) the State agency's duty to protect the privacy of household members` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2026 protect the privacy of household members in the longitudinal database`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency included personally identifiable information in the longitudinal database"

-- src:2628 | (i) protect the privacy of information about each member of each household that receives benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program in such State by ensuring that no personally identifiable information (including social security number, home address, or contact information) is included in the longitudinal database; and
@ref s 2026(n)(4)(B)(i) no personally identifiable information (src:2628)
GIVEN `the database includes personally identifiable information, including social security number, home address, or contact information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(4)(B)(i) the database protects the privacy of household members` MEANS
    IF `the database includes personally identifiable information, including social security number, home address, or contact information`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by ensuring that no personally identifiable information (including social security number, home address, or contact information) is included in the longitudinal database"
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "no personally identifiable information ... is included"

-- src:2629 | (ii) make the data under this paragraph available to researchers and the Secretary.
@ref s 2026(n)(4)(B)(ii) data available to researchers and the Secretary (src:2629)
`s 2026(n)(4)(B)(ii) the State agency's duty to make the data available` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2026 make the longitudinal database data available to researchers and the Secretary`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency did not make the data available to researchers and the Secretary"

-- src:2629 | (ii) make the data under this paragraph available to researchers and the Secretary.
@ref s 2026(n)(4)(B)(ii) the decision (src:2629)
GIVEN `the data are available to researchers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are available to the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(4)(B)(ii) the State has made the data available` MEANS
    IF `the data are available to researchers` AND `the data are available to the Secretary`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "make the data under this paragraph available to researchers and the Secretary"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the State shall do and not what follows if it does not

-- (n)(5) "The Secretary shall approve the establishment of longitudinal databases under paragraph (1) in States that— (A) meet the
-- requirements for databases under paragraph (3) and (4)(B); (B) reflect a range of participant numbers, demographics, operational
-- structures, and geographic regions; and (C) have the capacity to provide on a periodic and ongoing basis household and
-- participant data derived from the eligibility system and other data sources of the State."
-- src:2631 | The Secretary shall approve the establishment of longitudinal databases under paragraph (1) in States that—
@ref s 2026(n)(5) the Secretary's duty to approve (src:2631)
`s 2026(n)(5) the Secretary's duty to approve the establishment of longitudinal databases` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 approve the establishment of a longitudinal database`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not approve the establishment of a longitudinal database in a State that meets (A) to (C)"

-- src:2631 | The Secretary shall approve the establishment of longitudinal databases under paragraph (1) in States that—
-- src:2632 | (A) meet the requirements for databases under paragraph (3) and (4)(B);
-- src:2633 | (B) reflect a range of participant numbers, demographics, operational structures, and geographic regions; and
-- src:2634 | (C) have the capacity to provide on a periodic and ongoing basis household and participant data derived from the eligibility system and other data sources of the State.
@ref s 2026(n)(5) approval (src:2631-2634)
GIVEN `the State meets the requirements for databases under paragraphs (3) and (4)(B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State reflects a range of participant numbers, demographics, operational structures, and geographic regions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State has the capacity to provide, on a periodic and ongoing basis, household and participant data derived from the eligibility system and other data sources` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(5) the Secretary shall approve the establishment in the State` MEANS
    IF `the State meets the requirements for databases under paragraphs (3) and (4)(B)` AND `the State reflects a range of participant numbers, demographics, operational structures, and geographic regions` AND `the State has the capacity to provide, on a periodic and ongoing basis, household and participant data derived from the eligibility system and other data sources`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The Secretary shall approve the establishment of longitudinal databases under paragraph (1) in States that (A) ...; (B) ...; and (C)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "States that" meet (A) to (C); the text does not say the Secretary may not approve others

-- (n)(6) "(A) In carrying out this subsection, the Secretary may provide grants to States that have been approved by the Secretary in
-- accordance with paragraph (5) out of funds made available under paragraph (9). (B) Grants awarded under this paragraph shall be
-- made in such amounts and under such terms and conditions as the Secretary determines necessary to carry out the purposes of this subsection."
-- src:2637 | In carrying out this subsection, the Secretary may provide grants to States that have been approved by the Secretary in accordance with paragraph (5) out of funds made available under paragraph (9).
@ref s 2026(n)(6)(A) the Secretary's permission to provide grants (src:2637)
`s 2026(n)(6)(A) the Secretary's permission to provide grants to approved States` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MAY `s 2026 provide grants to approved States`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:2637 | In carrying out this subsection, the Secretary may provide grants to States that have been approved by the Secretary in accordance with paragraph (5) out of funds made available under paragraph (9).
@ref s 2026(n)(6)(A) approved States (src:2637)
GIVEN `the State has been approved by the Secretary in accordance with paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(6)(A) the Secretary may provide a grant to the State` MEANS
    IF `the State has been approved by the Secretary in accordance with paragraph (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the Secretary may provide grants to States that have been approved by the Secretary in accordance with paragraph (5)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to States that have been approved"

-- src:2639 | Grants awarded under this paragraph shall be made in such amounts and under such terms and conditions as the Secretary determines necessary to carry out the purposes of this subsection.
@ref s 2026(n)(6)(B) the amount (src:2639)
GIVEN `the amount the Secretary determines necessary to carry out the purposes of this subsection, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2026(n)(6)(B) the amount of the grant, in dollars` MEANS
    `the amount the Secretary determines necessary to carry out the purposes of this subsection, in dollars`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when not supplied: "in such amounts and under such terms and conditions as the Secretary determines necessary"

-- (n)(7) "(A) Not later than 4 years after the effective date of this subsection, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on
-- Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report on
-- the feasibility of expanding implementation of longitudinal databases to every State. (B) The report required under
-- subparagraph (A) shall describe— (i) the cost ...; (ii) the challenges and benefits ...; and (iii) alternatives ... and the
-- advantages and disadvantages of those alternatives."
-- src:2642 | Not later than 4 years after the effective date of this subsection, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report on the feasibility of expanding implementation of longitudinal databases to every State.
@ref s 2026(n)(7)(A) the Secretary's duty to report (src:2642)
`s 2026(n)(7)(A) the Secretary's duty to report on the feasibility of expanding longitudinal databases` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 submit the report on the feasibility of longitudinal databases to the Committees`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not submit the report on the feasibility of expanding longitudinal databases to every State"

-- src:2642 | Not later than 4 years after the effective date of this subsection, the Secretary shall submit to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report on the feasibility of expanding implementation of longitudinal databases to every State.
@ref s 2026(n)(7)(A) the date by which the report is due (src:2642)
GIVEN `the effective date of this subsection` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2026(n)(7)(A) the date by which the report is due` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the effective date of this subsection`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the effective date of the subsection is not in this text
    WHEN JUST effective THEN JUST (Date (DATE_DAY effective) (DATE_MONTH effective) (DATE_YEAR effective PLUS 4))   -- "Not later than 4 years after the effective date of this subsection"

-- src:2644 | The report required under subparagraph (A) shall describe—
-- src:2645 | (i) the cost of expanding implementation of longitudinal databases with consistent data to every State;
-- src:2646 | (ii) the challenges and benefits of using State longitudinal databases with consistent data; and
-- src:2647 | (iii) alternatives to expanding implementation of longitudinal databases with consistent data to every State that may achieve similar research outcomes and the advantages and disadvantages of those alternatives.
@ref s 2026(n)(7)(B) contents of the report (src:2644-2647)
GIVEN `the report describes the cost of expanding implementation of longitudinal databases with consistent data to every State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report describes the challenges and benefits of using State longitudinal databases with consistent data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report describes alternatives and the advantages and disadvantages of those alternatives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(7)(B) the report describes what the text requires` MEANS
    IF `the report describes the cost of expanding implementation of longitudinal databases with consistent data to every State` AND `the report describes the challenges and benefits of using State longitudinal databases with consistent data` AND `the report describes alternatives and the advantages and disadvantages of those alternatives`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall describe (i) the cost ...; (ii) the challenges and benefits ...; and (iii) alternatives ... and the advantages and disadvantages"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the report shall describe and not what follows if it does not

-- (n)(8) "Nothing in this subsection shall be construed to prevent or limit the ability of State agencies to establish or continue
-- operating databases used for purposes similar to the purposes outlined in this subsection."
-- src:2649 | Nothing in this subsection shall be construed to prevent or limit the ability of State agencies to establish or continue operating databases used for purposes similar to the purposes outlined in this subsection.
@ref s 2026(n)(8) effect (src:2649)
GIVEN `the database is used for purposes similar to the purposes outlined in this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(8) this subsection prevents or limits the State agency from operating the database` MEANS
    IF `the database is used for purposes similar to the purposes outlined in this subsection`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this subsection shall be construed to prevent or limit the ability of State agencies to establish or continue operating databases used for purposes similar"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only databases "used for purposes similar to the purposes outlined in this subsection"

-- (n)(9) "Of the funds made available under section 2027 of this title, the Secretary shall use to carry out this subsection— (A)
-- $20,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 to remain available through fiscal year 2021; and (B) $5,000,000 for fiscal year 2022 and each
-- fiscal year thereafter."
-- src:2651 | Of the funds made available under section 2027 of this title, the Secretary shall use to carry out this subsection—
@ref s 2026(n)(9) the Secretary's duty to use funds (src:2651)
`s 2026(n)(9) the Secretary's duty to use funds to carry out the longitudinal database subsection` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2026 use funds to carry out the longitudinal database subsection`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not use the funds the paragraph names to carry out the longitudinal database subsection"

-- src:2652 | (A) $20,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 to remain available through fiscal year 2021; and
-- src:2653 | (B) $5,000,000 for fiscal year 2022 and each fiscal year thereafter.
@ref s 2026(n)(9) the amount for the fiscal year (src:2652-2653)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2026(n)(9) the amount the Secretary shall use for the fiscal year, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fiscal year` EQUALS 2019 THEN JUST 20000000   -- "(A) $20,000,000 for fiscal year 2019"
        IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2022 THEN JUST 5000000   -- "(B) $5,000,000 for fiscal year 2022 and each fiscal year thereafter"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no amount for fiscal years 2020 and 2021 (the 2019 amount "remain[s] available through fiscal year 2021") or before 2019

-- src:2652 | (A) $20,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 to remain available through fiscal year 2021; and
@ref s 2026(n)(9)(A) availability of the fiscal year 2019 funds (src:2652)
GIVEN `fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2026(n)(9)(A) the fiscal year 2019 funds remain available in the fiscal year` MEANS
    IF `fiscal year` AT LEAST 2019 AND `fiscal year` AT MOST 2021
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "$20,000,000 for fiscal year 2019 to remain available through fiscal year 2021"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to remain available through fiscal year 2021"
